{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794847709148,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e72ffecbrpVf6MWZonWP","part":{"partID":"prt_1e54290c9001JvjQouCB5oBlT5","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e72ffecbrpVf6MWZonWP","messageID":"msg_1e541edd2001Wn6vWfJdVog0i7","type":"tool","id":"call_0c4c5581787743af9dc1855d","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cat .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-config.json; echo \"---STRAT TEMPLATE---\"; sed -n '1,120p' .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"{\n  \"topic\": \"\",\n  \"sessionId\": \"\",\n  \"parentSessionId\": null,\n  \"lineageMode\": \"new\",\n  \"generation\": 1,\n  \"continuedFromRun\": null,\n  \"migrationWindowEndsAt\": \"\",\n  \"maxIterations\": 7,\n  \"convergenceThreshold\": 0.10,\n  \"antiConvergence\": {\n    \"minIterations\": 2,\n    \"convergenceMode\": \"default\",\n    \"stopPolicy\": \"fail-closed\"\n  },\n  \"stuckThreshold\": 2,\n  \"maxDurationMinutes\": 120,\n  \"maxToolCallsPerIteration\": 24,\n  \"maxMinutesPerIteration\": 10,\n  \"progressiveSynthesis\": false,\n  \"specFolder\": \"\",\n  \"createdAt\": \"\",\n  \"status\": \"initialized\",\n  \"releaseReadinessState\": \"in-progress\",\n  \"executionMode\": \"auto\",\n  \"executor\": {\n    \"kind\": \"native\",\n    \"model\": null,\n    \"reasoningEffort\": null,\n    \"serviceTier\": null,\n    \"sandboxMode\": null,\n    \"timeoutSeconds\": 900\n  },\n  \"mode\": \"review\",\n  \"reviewTarget\": \"\",\n  \"reviewTargetType\": \"spec-folder\",\n  \"reviewDimensions\": [\n    \"correctness\",\n    \"security\",\n    \"traceability\",\n    \"maintainability\"\n  ],\n  \"reviewFocus\": null,\n  \"severityThreshold\": \"P2\",\n  \"crossReference\": {\n    \"core\": [\n      \"spec_code\",\n      \"checklist_evidence\"\n    ],\n    \"overlay\": [\n      \"skill_agent\",\n      \"agent_cross_runtime\",\n      \"feature_catalog_code\",\n      \"playbook_capability\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"qualityGateThreshold\": true,\n  \"runtimeCapabilityResolver\": \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/scripts/runtime-capabilities.cjs\",\n  \"reducerScriptPath\": \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs\",\n  \"fileProtection\": {\n    \"deep-review-config.json\": \"immutable\",\n    \"deep-review-state.jsonl\": \"append-only\",\n    \"deep-review-findings-registry.json\": \"auto-generated\",\n    \"deep-review-strategy.md\": \"mutable\",\n    \"deep-review-dashboard.md\": \"auto-generated\",\n    \".deep-review-pause\": \"operator-controlled\",\n    \"review-report.md\": \"mutable\",\n    \"review-report-v*.md\": \"write-once\",\n    \"iteration-*.md\": \"write-once\"\n  },\n  \"reducer\": {\n    \"enabled\": true,\n    \"inputs\": [\n      \"latestJSONLDelta\",\n      \"newIterationFile\",\n      \"priorReducedState\"\n    ],\n    \"outputs\": [\n      \"findingsRegistry\",\n      \"dashboardMetrics\",\n      \"strategyUpdates\"\n    ],\n    \"metrics\": [\n      \"dimensionsCovered\",\n      \"findingsBySeverity\",\n      \"openFindings\",\n      \"resolvedFindings\",\n      \"convergenceScore\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"_optimizerManaged\": {\n    \"description\": \"Fields managed by the offline loop optimizer (042.004). See optimizer-manifest.json for the canonical tunable/locked field registry.\",\n    \"manifestPath\": \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/optimizer/optimizer-manifest.json\",\n    \"tunableFields\": [\"convergenceThreshold\", \"stuckThreshold\", \"maxIterations\"],\n    \"lockedFields\": [\"lineageMode\", \"reducer\", \"fileProtection\", \"sessionId\", \"mode\", \"reviewDimensions\", \"antiConvergence.convergenceMode\", \"antiConvergence.stopPolicy\"],\n    \"promotionMode\": \"advisory-only\"\n  }\n}\n---STRAT TEMPLATE---\n---\ntitle: Deep Review Strategy Template\ndescription: Runtime template copied to review/ during initialization to track review progress, dimension coverage, findings, and outcomes across iterations.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"deep review strategy template\"\n  - \"review dimension tracking\"\n  - \"exhausted review approaches\"\n  - \"review session tracking\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: planning\nversion: 1.11.0.13\n---\n\n# Deep Review Strategy - Session Tracking Template\n\nRuntime template copied into the resolved `{artifact_dir}/` during initialization. Tracks review progress across iterations.\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nServes as the \"persistent brain\" for a deep review session. Records which dimensions remain, what was found (P0/P1/P2), what review approaches worked or failed, and where to focus next. Read by the orchestrator and agents at every iteration.\n\n### Usage\n\n- **Init:** Orchestrator copies this template to `{artifact_dir}/deep-review-strategy.md` and populates Topic, Review Dimensions, Known Context, and Review Boundaries from config and memory context.\n- **Per iteration:** Agent reads Next Focus, reviews the assigned dimension/files, updates findings, marks dimensions complete, and sets new Next Focus.\n- **Mutability:** Mutable, updated by both orchestrator and agents throughout the session.\n- **Protection:** None (shared mutable state). Orchestrator validates consistency on resume.\n- **Ownership:** Machine-managed metrics and coverage blocks are wrapped in explicit ownership markers. Human commentary and operator overrides live outside those markers.\n\n---\n\n## 2. TOPIC\n[Review target description from config -- set during initialization]\n\n---\n\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- [ ] D1 Correctness, Logic errors, off-by-one, wrong return types, broken invariants\n- [ ] D2 Security, Injection, auth bypass, secrets exposure, unsafe deserialization\n- [ ] D3 Traceability, Spec/code alignment, checklist evidence, cross-reference integrity\n- [ ] D4 Maintainability, Patterns, clarity, documentation quality, safe follow-on change cost\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n[What this review session is NOT trying to assess -- populated during initialization]\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n[Explicit conditions beyond convergence that should end the session -- populated during initialization]\n\n---\n\n## 6. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n[None yet -- populated as iterations complete dimension reviews]\n\n| Dimension | Verdict | Iteration | Summary |\n|-----------|---------|-----------|---------|\n| [D1 Correctness] | [PASS/CONDITIONAL/FAIL] | [N] | [1-sentence result] |\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 7. RUNNING FINDINGS\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- **P0 (Critical):** 0 active\n- **P1 (Major):** 0 active\n- **P2 (Minor):** 0 active\n- **Delta this iteration:** +0 P0, +0 P1, +0 P2\n\n[Findings are tracked in `deep-review-findings-registry.json`. This section provides a running count summary updated after each iteration.]\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n- [Approach]: [Why it worked] (iteration N)\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n- [Approach]: [Why it failed] (iteration N)\n\n---\n\n## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n[Populated when a review approach has been tried from multiple angles without yielding new findings]\n\n### [Category Name] -- BLOCKED (iteration N, N attempts)\n- What was tried: [specific review approaches attempted]\n- Why blocked: [root cause of exhaustion]\n- Do NOT retry: [explicit prohibition]\n\n### [Category Name] -- PRODUCTIVE (iteration N)\n- What worked: [successful review approaches in this category]\n- Prefer for: [related dimensions where this category may help]\n\n---\n\n## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Swept: none yet\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"topic\": \"\",\n  \"sessionId\": \"\",\n  \"parentSessionId\": null,\n  \"lineageMode\": \"new\",\n  \"generation\": 1,\n  \"continuedFromRun\": null,\n  \"migrationWindowEndsAt\": \"\",\n  \"maxIterations\": 7,\n  \"convergenceThreshold\": 0.10,\n  \"antiConvergence\": {\n    \"minIterations\": 2,\n    \"convergenceMode\": \"default\",\n    \"stopPolicy\": \"fail-closed\"\n  },\n  \"stuckThreshold\": 2,\n  \"maxDurationMinutes\": 120,\n  \"maxToolCallsPerIteration\": 24,\n  \"maxMinutesPerIteration\": 10,\n  \"progressiveSynthesis\": false,\n  \"specFolder\": \"\",\n  \"createdAt\": \"\",\n  \"status\": \"initialized\",\n  \"releaseReadinessState\": \"in-progress\",\n  \"executionMode\": \"auto\",\n  \"executor\": {\n    \"kind\": \"native\",\n    \"model\": null,\n    \"reasoningEffort\": null,\n    \"serviceTier\": null,\n    \"sandboxMode\": null,\n    \"timeoutSeconds\": 900\n  },\n  \"mode\": \"review\",\n  \"reviewTarget\": \"\",\n  \"reviewTargetType\": \"spec-folder\",\n  \"reviewDimensions\": [\n    \"correctness\",\n    \"security\",\n    \"traceability\",\n    \"maintainability\"\n  ],\n  \"reviewFocus\": null,\n  \"severityThreshold\": \"P2\",\n  \"crossReference\": {\n    \"core\": [\n      \"spec_code\",\n      \"checklist_evidence\"\n    ],\n    \"overlay\": [\n      \"skill_agent\",\n      \"agent_cross_runtime\",\n      \"feature_catalog_code\",\n      \"playbook_capability\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"qualityGateThreshold\": true,\n  \"runtimeCapabilityResolver\": \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/scripts/runtime-capabilities.cjs\",\n  \"reducerScriptPath\": \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs\",\n  \"fileProtection\": {\n    \"deep-review-config.json\": \"immutable\",\n    \"deep-review-state.jsonl\": \"append-only\",\n    \"deep-review-findings-registry.json\": \"auto-generated\",\n    \"deep-review-strategy.md\": \"mutable\",\n    \"deep-review-dashboard.md\": \"auto-generated\",\n    \".deep-review-pause\": \"operator-controlled\",\n    \"review-report.md\": \"mutable\",\n    \"review-report-v*.md\": \"write-once\",\n    \"iteration-*.md\": \"write-once\"\n  },\n  \"reducer\": {\n    \"enabled\": true,\n    \"inputs\": [\n      \"latestJSONLDelta\",\n      \"newIterationFile\",\n      \"priorReducedState\"\n    ],\n    \"outputs\": [\n      \"findingsRegistry\",\n      \"dashboardMetrics\",\n      \"strategyUpdates\"\n    ],\n    \"metrics\": [\n      \"dimensionsCovered\",\n      \"findingsBySeverity\",\n      \"openFindings\",\n      \"resolvedFindings\",\n      \"convergenceScore\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"_optimizerManaged\": {\n    \"description\": \"Fields managed by the offline loop optimizer (042.004). See optimizer-manifest.json for the canonical tunable/locked field registry.\",\n    \"manifestPath\": \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/optimizer/optimizer-manifest.json\",\n    \"tunableFields\": [\"convergenceThreshold\", \"stuckThreshold\", \"maxIterations\"],\n    \"lockedFields\": [\"lineageMode\", \"reducer\", \"fileProtection\", \"sessionId\", \"mode\", \"reviewDimensions\", \"antiConvergence.convergenceMode\", \"antiConvergence.stopPolicy\"],\n    \"promotionMode\": \"advisory-only\"\n  }\n}\n---STRAT TEMPLATE---\n---\ntitle: Deep Review Strategy Template\ndescription: Runtime template copied to review/ during initialization to track review progress, dimension coverage, findings, and outcomes across iterations.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"deep review strategy template\"\n  - \"review dimension tracking\"\n  - \"exhausted review approaches\"\n  - \"review session tracking\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: planning\nversion: 1.11.0.13\n---\n\n# Deep Review Strategy - Session Tracking Template\n\nRuntime template copied into the resolved `{artifact_dir}/` during initialization. Tracks review progress across iterations.\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nServes as the \"persistent brain\" for a deep review session. Records which dimensions remain, what was found (P0/P1/P2), what review approaches worked or failed, and where to focus next. Read by the orchestrator and agents at every iteration.\n\n### Usage\n\n- **Init:** Orchestrator copies this template to `{artifact_dir}/deep-review-strategy.md` and populates Topic, Review Dimensions, Known Context, and Review Boundaries from config and memory context.\n- **Per iteration:** Agent reads Next Focus, reviews the assigned dimension/files, updates findings, marks dimensions complete, and sets new Next Focus.\n- **Mutability:** Mutable, updated by both orchestrator and agents throughout the session.\n- **Protection:** None (shared mutable state). Orchestrator validates consistency on resume.\n- **Ownership:** Machine-managed metrics and coverage blocks are wrapped in explicit ownership markers. Human commentary and operator overrides live outside those markers.\n\n---\n\n## 2. TOPIC\n[Review target description from config -- set during initialization]\n\n---\n\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- [ ] D1 Correctness, Logic errors, off-by-one, wrong return types, broken invariants\n- [ ] D2 Security, Injection, auth bypass, secrets exposure, unsafe deserialization\n- [ ] D3 Traceability, Spec/code alignment, checklist evidence, cross-reference integrity\n- [ ] D4 Maintainability, Patterns, clarity, documentation quality, safe follow-on change cost\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n[What this review session is NOT trying to assess -- populated during initialization]\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n[Explicit conditions beyond convergence that should end the session -- populated during initialization]\n\n---\n\n## 6. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n[None yet -- populated as iterations complete dimension reviews]\n\n| Dimension | Verdict | Iteration | Summary |\n|-----------|---------|-----------|---------|\n| [D1 Correctness] | [PASS/CONDITIONAL/FAIL] | [N] | [1-sentence result] |\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 7. RUNNING FINDINGS\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- **P0 (Critical):** 0 active\n- **P1 (Major):** 0 active\n- **P2 (Minor):** 0 active\n- **Delta this iteration:** +0 P0, +0 P1, +0 P2\n\n[Findings are tracked in `deep-review-findings-registry.json`. This section provides a running count summary updated after each iteration.]\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n- [Approach]: [Why it worked] (iteration N)\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n- [Approach]: [Why it failed] (iteration N)\n\n---\n\n## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n[Populated when a review approach has been tried from multiple angles without yielding new findings]\n\n### [Category Name] -- BLOCKED (iteration N, N attempts)\n- What was tried: [specific review approaches attempted]\n- Why blocked: [root cause of exhaustion]\n- Do NOT retry: [explicit prohibition]\n\n### [Category Name] -- PRODUCTIVE (iteration N)\n- What worked: [successful review approaches in this category]\n- Prefer for: [related dimensions where this category may help]\n\n---\n\n## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Swept: none yet\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cat .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-config.json; echo \\\"---STRAT TEMPLATE---\\\"; sed -n '1,120p' .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794847707337,"end":1794847709148}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794847709188,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e72ffecbrpVf6MWZonWP","part":{"partID":"prt_1e54294300010pPu3xWPn5RhNw","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e72ffecbrpVf6MWZonWP","messageID":"msg_1e541edd2001Wn6vWfJdVog0i7","type":"tool","id":"call_b2c56ce305eb4f0b9a1bef8d","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"sed -n '400,470p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts; echo \"---USES---\"; rg -n \"commandOnlyMentioned\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime --glob '!tests/**' | head -20","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"// A question often names the command after `the`, as in `is the /x command safe`.\nexport const COMMAND_BARE_ASK_LEAD = '(?:is|does|can|will|would) (?:the )?';\n\n// A clause that opens with a use verb and `it` asks for the command an earlier\n// clause only named, so a naming such as `not run /x yet, please start it`\n// becomes a request. The clause has to open that way so `I will run it` stays a\n// statement.\nconst COMMAND_ASKED_BY_PRONOUN = new RegExp(`(?:^|[,.;!?\\\\n]) *(?:(?:and|then|so|please|now|just|go ahead and) )*${COMMAND_USE_VERB} it\\\\b`);\n\n// A prompt names a command to refuse it or to ask about it as often as it names\n// one to run it, so an offer must read the naming before it trusts the name. The\n// text is folded first, because a keyed apostrophe or a run of spaces must not\n// hide the lead, while a line break survives as the sentence end it is. Inline\n// code, bold and quote marks around a name are dropped for the same reason, so a\n// refusal of a backticked command reads as the plain refusal does. An underscore\n// stays, because a command name may hold one. The\n// boundary before the lead keeps a command name from matching inside a word or a\n// path, and the boundary after it keeps a longer command name from reading as the\n// shorter one. Every occurrence has to carry a lead, because one led naming does\n// not turn a later unled naming into a request.\nexport function commandOnlyMentioned(prompt: string, command: string): boolean {\n  const text = prompt\n    .toLowerCase()\n    .replace(/[`*\"\\u201c\\u201d]/g, '')\n    .replace(/[\\u2018\\u2019]/g, \"'\")\n    .replace(/[^\\S\\n]+/g, ' ')\n    .replace(/ *\\n\\s*/g, '\\n');\n  const name = escapePhrase(command.toLowerCase());\n  const occurrences = [...text.matchAll(new RegExp(`(?:^|[^a-z0-9_/])${name}(?![a-z0-9_-])`, 'g'))];\n  if (occurrences.length === 0) return false;\n  return occurrences.every((occurrence) => {\n    const nameEnd = (occurrence.index ?? 0) + occurrence[0].length;\n    const before = text.slice(0, nameEnd);\n    const tail = text.slice(nameEnd);\n    if (COMMAND_ASKED_BY_PRONOUN.test(tail.split(/(?:^|[\\s,;(])\\/[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*(?::[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*)?(?![a-z0-9_\\/-]|\\.[a-z0-9])/)[0])) return false;\n    const led = COMMAND_DECLINE_LEADS.some((lead) => (\n      new RegExp(`(?:^|[^a-z0-9_/])${lead}${COMMAND_OR_LIST}${name}$`).test(before)\n    )) || COMMAND_ASK_LEADS.some((lead) => (\n      new RegExp(`(?:^|[^a-z0-9_/])${lead}${COMMAND_OR_LIST}${name}$`).test(before)\n    ));\n    if (led) return true;\n    const bareLead = new RegExp(`(?:^|[^a-z0-9_/])${COMMAND_BARE_ASK_LEAD}${COMMAND_OR_LIST}${name}$`).test(before);\n    if (!bareLead) return false;\n    const sentenceEnd = tail.search(/[.!\\n]/);\n    const sentence = sentenceEnd === -1 ? tail : tail.slice(0, sentenceEnd);\n    // A chat question often leaves the question mark off, so a bare ask word that\n    // opens a sentence still asks about the command.\n    return sentence.includes('?')\n      || new RegExp(`(?:^|[.!?\\\\n] *)${COMMAND_BARE_ASK_LEAD}${COMMAND_OR_LIST}${name}$`).test(before);\n  });\n}\n\n// A compiled route arrives as unvalidated JSON from a separate process, so the\n// shape is narrowed here rather than trusted. Arrays count as objects in\n// JavaScript and would let `action` read off an unrelated field, so they are\n// excluded explicitly.\nfunction asRecord(value: unknown): Record<string, unknown> | undefined {\n  if (typeof value !== 'object' || value === null || Array.isArray(value)) return undefined;\n  return value as Record<string, unknown>;\n}\n\n// The command for a hub's recommendation, or undefined when the route does not\n// single out one mode. Only a single-mode route names a command unambiguously:\n// a bundle or a multi-target route has more than one answer, and asking the\n// reader to pick belongs to the recommend path, not here. Never throws, because\n// a missing command must degrade to \"no command offered\" rather than break\n// routing. The prompt decides whether a costly deep-loop command is offered at\n// all: a reader who only asks about the topic gets no command, rather than one\n// that would launch work they never requested.\nexport function attachCommand(\n  skillId: string,\n---USES---\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:259:  if (commandOnlyMentioned(prompt, command)) return undefined;\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:420:export function commandOnlyMentioned(prompt: string, command: string): boolean {\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:501:  if (commandOnlyMentioned(prompt, commands[workflowMode])) return undefined;\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:22:  commandOnlyMentioned,\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1213:    if (command === undefined || !commandOnlyMentioned(prompt, command)) return recommendation;\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1232:      && !commandOnlyMentioned(promptLower, base)) return recommendation;\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1248:  if (commandOnlyMentioned(promptLower, command)) return [...ranked];\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md:148:| `command-attach.ts` | `attachCommand()` names the slash command for a hub recommendation whose compiled route picks one `workflowMode`. It reads the `MODE_COMMANDS` table that `derive-command-bridges.cjs` generates from each hub's `mode-registry.json`. A `system-deep-loop` command needs the same command typed in the prompt or a `DEPTH_WORDING` phrase, and a prompt that matches `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` gets no command. `commandOnlyMentioned()` reads how the prompt names a command, and a command the prompt refuses or asks about is not offered unless a later clause asks for it. A correction inside an existing document carries no `/create:readme`, `/create:feature-catalog` or `/create:manual-testing-playbook`. The module has no imports. |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:16:  commandOnlyMentioned,\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:140:    expect(commandOnlyMentioned(prompt, command)).toBe(true);\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:144:    expect(commandOnlyMentioned(prompt, command)).toBe(true);\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:148:    expect(commandOnlyMentioned(prompt, command)).toBe(false);\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:152:    expect(commandOnlyMentioned(prompt, command)).toBe(false);\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:169:    expect(commandOnlyMentioned(prompt, command)).toBe(true);\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:179:    expect(commandOnlyMentioned(prompt, command)).toBe(true);\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:183:    expect(commandOnlyMentioned('run `/create:readme` for the advisor skill', '/create:readme')).toBe(false);\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:197:    expect(commandOnlyMentioned(prompt, command)).toBe(false);\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:211:    expect(commandOnlyMentioned(prompt, command)).toBe(false);\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:224:    expect(commandOnlyMentioned(prompt, command)).toBe(true);\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:232:    expect(commandOnlyMentioned(prompt, command)).toBe(true);\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"// A question often names the command after `the`, as in `is the /x command safe`.\nexport const COMMAND_BARE_ASK_LEAD = '(?:is|does|can|will|would) (?:the )?';\n\n// A clause that opens with a use verb and `it` asks for the command an earlier\n// clause only named, so a naming such as `not run /x yet, please start it`\n// becomes a request. The clause has to open that way so `I will run it` stays a\n// statement.\nconst COMMAND_ASKED_BY_PRONOUN = new RegExp(`(?:^|[,.;!?\\\\n]) *(?:(?:and|then|so|please|now|just|go ahead and) )*${COMMAND_USE_VERB} it\\\\b`);\n\n// A prompt names a command to refuse it or to ask about it as often as it names\n// one to run it, so an offer must read the naming before it trusts the name. The\n// text is folded first, because a keyed apostrophe or a run of spaces must not\n// hide the lead, while a line break survives as the sentence end it is. Inline\n// code, bold and quote marks around a name are dropped for the same reason, so a\n// refusal of a backticked command reads as the plain refusal does. An underscore\n// stays, because a command name may hold one. The\n// boundary before the lead keeps a command name from matching inside a word or a\n// path, and the boundary after it keeps a longer command name from reading as the\n// shorter one. Every occurrence has to carry a lead, because one led naming does\n// not turn a later unled naming into a request.\nexport function commandOnlyMentioned(prompt: string, command: string): boolean {\n  const text = prompt\n    .toLowerCase()\n    .replace(/[`*\"\\u201c\\u201d]/g, '')\n    .replace(/[\\u2018\\u2019]/g, \"'\")\n    .replace(/[^\\S\\n]+/g, ' ')\n    .replace(/ *\\n\\s*/g, '\\n');\n  const name = escapePhrase(command.toLowerCase());\n  const occurrences = [...text.matchAll(new RegExp(`(?:^|[^a-z0-9_/])${name}(?![a-z0-9_-])`, 'g'))];\n  if (occurrences.length === 0) return false;\n  return occurrences.every((occurrence) => {\n    const nameEnd = (occurrence.index ?? 0) + occurrence[0].length;\n    const before = text.slice(0, nameEnd);\n    const tail = text.slice(nameEnd);\n    if (COMMAND_ASKED_BY_PRONOUN.test(tail.split(/(?:^|[\\s,;(])\\/[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*(?::[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*)?(?![a-z0-9_\\/-]|\\.[a-z0-9])/)[0])) return false;\n    const led = COMMAND_DECLINE_LEADS.some((lead) => (\n      new RegExp(`(?:^|[^a-z0-9_/])${lead}${COMMAND_OR_LIST}${name}$`).test(before)\n    )) || COMMAND_ASK_LEADS.some((lead) => (\n      new RegExp(`(?:^|[^a-z0-9_/])${lead}${COMMAND_OR_LIST}${name}$`).test(before)\n    ));\n    if (led) return true;\n    const bareLead = new RegExp(`(?:^|[^a-z0-9_/])${COMMAND_BARE_ASK_LEAD}${COMMAND_OR_LIST}${name}$`).test(before);\n    if (!bareLead) return false;\n    const sentenceEnd = tail.search(/[.!\\n]/);\n    const sentence = sentenceEnd === -1 ? tail : tail.slice(0, sentenceEnd);\n    // A chat question often leaves the question mark off, so a bare ask word that\n    // opens a sentence still asks about the command.\n    return sentence.includes('?')\n      || new RegExp(`(?:^|[.!?\\\\n] *)${COMMAND_BARE_ASK_LEAD}${COMMAND_OR_LIST}${name}$`).test(before);\n  });\n}\n\n// A compiled route arrives as unvalidated JSON from a separate process, so the\n// shape is narrowed here rather than trusted. Arrays count as objects in\n// JavaScript and would let `action` read off an unrelated field, so they are\n// excluded explicitly.\nfunction asRecord(value: unknown): Record<string, unknown> | undefined {\n  if (typeof value !== 'object' || value === null || Array.isArray(value)) return undefined;\n  return value as Record<string, unknown>;\n}\n\n// The command for a hub's recommendation, or undefined when the route does not\n// single out one mode. Only a single-mode route names a command unambiguously:\n// a bundle or a multi-target route has more than one answer, and asking the\n// reader to pick belongs to the recommend path, not here. Never throws, because\n// a missing command must degrade to \"no command offered\" rather than break\n// routing. The prompt decides whether a costly deep-loop command is offered at\n// all: a reader who only asks about the topic gets no command, rather than one\n// that would launch work they never requested.\nexport function attachCommand(\n  skillId: string,\n---USES---\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:259:  if (commandOnlyMentioned(prompt, command)) return undefined;\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:420:export function commandOnlyMentioned(prompt: string, command: string): boolean {\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:501:  if (commandOnlyMentioned(prompt, commands[workflowMode])) return undefined;\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:22:  commandOnlyMentioned,\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1213:    if (command === undefined || !commandOnlyMentioned(prompt, command)) return recommendation;\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1232:      && !commandOnlyMentioned(promptLower, base)) return recommendation;\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1248:  if (commandOnlyMentioned(promptLower, command)) return [...ranked];\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md:148:| `command-attach.ts` | `attachCommand()` names the slash command for a hub recommendation whose compiled route picks one `workflowMode`. It reads the `MODE_COMMANDS` table that `derive-command-bridges.cjs` generates from each hub's `mode-registry.json`. A `system-deep-loop` command needs the same command typed in the prompt or a `DEPTH_WORDING` phrase, and a prompt that matches `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` gets no command. `commandOnlyMentioned()` reads how the prompt names a command, and a command the prompt refuses or asks about is not offered unless a later clause asks for it. A correction inside an existing document carries no `/create:readme`, `/create:feature-catalog` or `/create:manual-testing-playbook`. The module has no imports. |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:16:  commandOnlyMentioned,\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:140:    expect(commandOnlyMentioned(prompt, command)).toBe(true);\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:144:    expect(commandOnlyMentioned(prompt, command)).toBe(true);\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:148:    expect(commandOnlyMentioned(prompt, command)).toBe(false);\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:152:    expect(commandOnlyMentioned(prompt, command)).toBe(false);\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:169:    expect(commandOnlyMentioned(prompt, command)).toBe(true);\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:179:    expect(commandOnlyMentioned(prompt, command)).toBe(true);\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:183:    expect(commandOnlyMentioned('run `/create:readme` for the advisor skill', '/create:readme')).toBe(false);\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:197:    expect(commandOnlyMentioned(prompt, command)).toBe(false);\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:211:    expect(commandOnlyMentioned(prompt, command)).toBe(false);\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:224:    expect(commandOnlyMentioned(prompt, command)).toBe(true);\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:232:    expect(commandOnlyMentioned(prompt, command)).toBe(true);\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"sed -n '400,470p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts; echo \\\"---USES---\\\"; rg -n \\\"commandOnlyMentioned\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime --glob '!tests/**' | head -20\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794847708208,"end":1794847709188}}}}
