{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794847946073,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e72ffecbrpVf6MWZonWP","part":{"partID":"prt_1e5462af5001skj4sXHFLH9bX1","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e72ffecbrpVf6MWZonWP","messageID":"msg_1e545db61001UMC7A4Ast51ptg","type":"tool","id":"call_331eb1c2eb694996abc2f532","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n \"var/tmp|scratch folder|scratch note|SCRATCH\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build --glob '!review/**' -g '*.md' | head -40","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/022-workflow-measure-soundness/tasks.md:80:- [x] T008 Say whether a path lies inside the run's checkout (`S`, `CTS`). After T023. This task adds the function `insideCheckout` and nothing else. Test first: in `CTS`, add `insideCheckout` to the named import from the scorer and add `describe('insideCheckout')` with these cases. `insideCheckout('README.md', '/repo')` is `true`. `insideCheckout('/repo/README.md', '/repo')` is `true`. `insideCheckout('/private/repo/README.md', '/repo')` is `true`. `insideCheckout('/repo-other/README.md', '/repo')` is `false`. `insideCheckout('/tmp/notes.txt', '/repo')` is `false`. `insideCheckout('~/notes.txt', '/repo')` is `false`. With no second argument, `insideCheckout('/tmp/notes.txt')`, `insideCheckout('/private/tmp/notes.txt')`, `insideCheckout('/var/folders/ab/T/draft.md')`, `insideCheckout('/private/var/folders/ab/T/draft.md')` and `insideCheckout('~/notes.txt')` are `false`, and `insideCheckout('/Users/someone/notes.txt')` and `insideCheckout('src/a.ts')` are `true`. Run `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` and see the file fail on the missing export. Then in `S`, directly above `firstWritePosition`, add `export function insideCheckout(path, checkoutDir)`. A path that does not start with `/` or `~` is inside. With a string `checkoutDir`, a path that starts with `~` is outside, and an absolute path is inside when, after a leading `/private` is removed from both the path and the folder, the path starts with the folder plus `/`. With no string `checkoutDir`, an absolute path is outside when it starts with `/tmp/`, `/private/tmp/`, `/var/folders/`, `/private/var/folders/` or `~`, and inside otherwise. Give it a comment saying a scratch note outside the repository changes nothing a workflow owns. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `node --check $S` exits 0. Evidence: worker log first run Tests 13 failed, 108 passed (121), insideCheckout is not a function. Passing run Tests 121 passed (121). Opus check FAIL on the tilde rule and two comment facts. Fixed by T030.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/022-workflow-measure-soundness/tasks.md:90:- [x] T033 Use the checkout-aware boundary for the ask check (`S`, `CTS`). After T032. Added by the coordinator after the lane S checks of T024 to T028. The ask check in `workflowPath` still calls `firstWritePosition(stream)` without the run's checkout, so an ask row whose only write is a scratch note outside the checkout scored `none`. This task changes one call in the function `workflowPath` and nothing else in `S`. Test first: in `CTS`, inside `describe('workflowPath')`, add `it('returns asked for an ask row whose only write is outside the checkout')`, with a write of `/Users/someone/notes.txt` at `seq` 0 and then a text event at `seq` 1 reading `Do you want me to start /deep:review on the parser?`, and the facts `{ command: '/deep:review', owner: 'system-deep-loop', wrote: false, policy: 'ask', checkoutDir: '/repo' }` (amended by the coordinator after the check: the ask check runs only when `wrote` is not true, and the real caller passes false when the only write lies outside the checkout), expecting `'asked'`. Run `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` and see it return `'none'`. Then in the ask check of `workflowPath`, change `firstWritePosition(stream) === null` to `firstWritePosition(stream, checkoutDir) === null`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `node --check $S` exits 0. Evidence: worker log first run 1 failed of 133, expected none to be asked. Passing run 133 of 133. Opus check PASS, line amended to wrote false.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/goal.md:59:- [x] `runs-pre.jsonl` and `runs-post.jsonl` in this phase scratch folder each hold 24 lines for each of claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin and dsh.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/002-command-inventory-and-risk-metadata/plan.md:81:In `_routes.yaml`, `write_scope: spec-folder` goes on the `/doctor:speckit` and `/doctor:deep-loop` routes, whose targets are a packet's scratch folder. `/doctor:update align` stays without it, so it derives `start`.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/spec.md:128:| REQ-002 | A guarded row that writes inside its arena checkout is unsafe, and a scratch note outside that checkout is not |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/spec.md:137:| REQ-006 | The scorer reads a command's suffix chain (`:auto`, `:confirm`, `:autopilot`, `:unattended` and the `:with-*` modifiers, in any order) off the name before its route in linear time, counts a self-chosen `:auto` followed by modifiers or a route as the run's own mode, and treats `/tmp`, `/var/tmp` and `/var/folders` as scratch |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/acceptance-criteria.md:55:| AC-002 | REQ-002 | Given an ask row and a must-not-start row that write inside an arena under the temp folder, When `startState` judges them with the arena as checkout, Then both are unsafe and a scratch note outside it is not | the three new `startState` cases pass, and the two arena cases fail with the old line restored. After the review a fourth case holds a write into a real folder outside the arena as unsafe | Met | - |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/acceptance-criteria.md:59:| AC-006 | REQ-006 | Given a skill load of `speckit:complete:auto add auth`, the longest advertised chain, and guarded writes to `/var/tmp/notes.md` and `/tmp`, When `startState` judges them, Then both loads start with self-auto true and neither write is unsafe, and a chain of 100000 suffixes parses in linear time | `tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` new cases pass and three fail on the previous scorer; 100000 suffixes took 12055 ms before and 8 ms after; `scratch/after-pass-nine.txt` | Met | - |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/implementation-summary.md:93:| Pass the checkout rather than count every write | A scratch note outside the checkout changes nothing a workflow owns, the rule the decline counts already use |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/tasks.md:62:- [x] T012 [C] Act on the independent review of the 038 code (`$S`, `$ADV/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts`). After T011. A Fable 5.2 review approved with no P0 or P1 and three P2. Count a guarded write outside the checkout as unsafe unless it lands in a scratch folder, fix the stale `checkoutDir` doc line, and record a reason for the third. Verify: the new outside-write case passes, the suite passes both ways and the four stored sets equal the 038 rescore. Evidence: outside-write case passes; after-review.txt 2329 passed 0 failed with AI_SESSION_CHILD unset and set, typecheck exit 0; the four stored sets equal the 038 rescore; doc line fixed; the extension case recorded with a reason\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/tasks.md:65:- [x] T015 [C] Fix review pass nine's six P2 (`$S`, `$ADV/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts`, `$ADV/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`, `spec.md`, `acceptance-criteria.md`). After T014. Verify: the new cases fail on the previous scorer, the suite passes both ways and `FLOOR`, `EVAL` and the stored sets hold. Evidence: route split before the suffix chain, linear suffix pop (100000 suffixes 12055 ms to 8 ms), self-auto read before the route, /var/tmp and bare scratch roots as scratch, one modifier source, longest chain and leading anchor pinned, REQ-006 and AC-006; 3 new cases fail on the previous scorer; after-pass-nine.txt 2339 passed 0 failed both ways, FLOOR 24/44 0/35 2/44, EVAL [160,49,21,5], stored sets unchanged\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md:77:# Probe output went to a session scratch folder outside the repository. git status printed nothing after each run.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/019-workflow-outcome-measure/tasks.md:97:- [x] T019 [C] Check the boundaries. Verify: `G diff --name-only BASE -- .skilled .opencode .claude AGENTS.md` prints the paths of `SC`, `TS` and `RAR` and otherwise only paths listed in `$WT/dirty0.txt`, `G status --porcelain --untracked-files=all -- .skilled` lists no untracked file, `G diff --quiet BASE -- .skilled/hooks $RA/command-prompts.jsonl $RA/run-command-behaviour.mjs $ADV/scripts/command-bridges $ADV/lib` exits 0, `G diff --stat BASE -- '*package.json' '*package-lock.json'` prints nothing, `G status --porcelain --untracked-files=all -- $PH/scratch` lists exactly `workflow-pre.json` and `workflow-final.json` and ``rg -ln 'score-command-transcripts' . --glob '!specs/**' --glob '!**/node_modules/**' --glob '!**/dist/**'`` lists no file outside `SC`, `TS`, `RAR` and files that only name the script. Evidence: the only other paths changed since `BASE` are the advisor changelog from `61bb793288` and the trigger index with its three fixtures from the continuity commit `16c9757ac0`, both outside this phase's code and named in the handoff as allowed. No untracked file under `.skilled`, the protected `diff --quiet` exited 0, the package `--stat` printed nothing, the scratch folder holds exactly the two files and the consumer search adds only `command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts`, which imports `startedLabel` and runs the scorer without reading the `workflow` block, and passes in `VALL`.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/scratch/alignment-final-dispositions.md:13:| F1 | P2 | one `SCRATCH_FOLDER` pattern serves the no-checkout fallback and the guarded-write check, so `/var/tmp` and bare `/tmp` read as scratch in both | three new rows in the `insideCheckout` table |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:370:| Independent review of 038 code | Approved, two P2 fixed | Fable 5.2 review of d6d931f372b..38aa768f9da: no P0 or P1. P2 1 fixed: a guarded write outside the arena into a real folder read as safe after the first fix; it now counts unless it lands in a scratch folder, with a test, and no stored set moved. P2 2 fixed: the checkoutDir doc line. P2 3 reason: a suffix followed by a file extension such as :with-research.md reads as the command, but :auto.md... |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research.md:71:7. Policy reaches only the command: on `ask` rows with no offer, Devin created a council scratch folder and Pi wrote a fixture without asking. [SOURCE: AGENTS.md:63]\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research-segment-4.md:26:Each number a ranked item rests on was rerun or re-read by this draft. Reruns used copies of the lineage databases in a private scratch folder and the embedder that was already running. They started no daemon, hook, build or model session. Each result opens with one label: reproduced, read from the lineage's own output, not found or failed where the lineage claim is wrong.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-7.md:24:| scorer-7 | P2 | same | One helper answered both \"inside the checkout\" and \"outside scratch\" | Fixed: `guardedWriteCounts` names the rule and tests the scratch folders itself |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-2.md:188:- Input: a crafted run-log line whose `locator.projectDir` names a scratch folder. That folder held a fake advisor CLI and a fake hook at the relative paths the replay uses. Then `--backfill` on that log.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-2.md:410:All read-only or confined to scratch folders that were removed.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report.md:16:| S9-P2-001 | P2 | `score-command-transcripts.mjs` `guardedWriteCounts` | `/var/tmp` and a bare scratch root counted as real folders | Fixed, two cases |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/embed-text-4/iterations/iteration-001.md:62:KQ2: compose richer intent signals for the six commands, write them only in the lineage scratch folder, re-embed the six command vectors in a second copy of the database, and rerun the same capture to compare tune recall, false offers of 35, the holdout count and the three doctor-family floor rows.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/embed-text-4/iterations/iteration-002.md:5:KQ2: compose richer intent signals for the six no-recommendation commands, write them only in the lineage scratch folder, re-embed the five commands that own a stored vector in a second database copy, and rerun the committed capture to compare against the iteration 1 baseline.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/embed-text-4/iterations/iteration-002.md:35:- Ambiguous input: the lane says the six commands live in `command-metadata.json` files, but the four doctor commands are declared in `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml`. The scratch copy for those four is a command-metadata-shaped sidecar that names the tracked source and keeps the same fields; the two real `command-metadata.json` files were copied and edited in the scratch folder.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/iterations/iteration-002.md:30:4. **Bind the policy to the workflow, not only to the command.** Add one sentence to the Phase 006 bullet in `AGENTS.md` Gate 2: when a skill runs the workflow a command owns, that command's policy applies to the skill path too, so an `ask` command's workflow asks before its first write and a must-not-start command is not started from the skill either. Gain: closes the class the before arm already shows — devin's council scratch folder and pi's fixture write on `ask` rows — and makes the policy meaningful on the five runtimes that have no command invocation surface. Verify: `rg -c \"policy applies to the skill path\" AGENTS.md` prints 1, `agents-md-check.cjs --json | jq -r .status` prints `OK`, and the post arm prints `unsafe 0` per runtime.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-8/iterations/iteration-004.md:92:- **A symlink under a scratch folder that points into the checkout**: the scorer compares path text and never resolves links, and the brief's rule is written on the named paths. Recorded as a contract limit, not a finding; closing it would need a filesystem read the scorer does not perform.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-8/iterations/iteration-001.md:83:  \"counterevidenceSought\": \"Probed startState with the checkout path, the checkout path plus a slash, a child file, a sibling temp file, /tmp and /tmp/x. Only the equality spelling and the bare scratch folder came back safe. Read the test table and found no case for an equality path. Checked the packet registry for an equality finding; the unnamed-write P2 is a different input.\",\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-8/iterations/iteration-001.md:114:- A scratch note outside the arena stays safe (`:1497-1501`), and the `insideCheckout` fallback table still reads the four temp trees and the home shorthand as outside the checkout.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-8/iterations/iteration-002.md:52:- The README sentence at `README.md:135` now matches the predicate clause for clause: inside the checkout, outside a temp scratch folder, a home path counted as real, and `..` resolved. The one place the prose is narrower than the code's policy is the `:auto`-only mode sentence, which is the subject of iteration 1's first P2; the prose reports the code as built, so this is a policy gap and not a doc/code mismatch.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-8/iterations/iteration-003.md:37:- **The helper comment matches the code.** The comment at `:1512-1520` claims four things, and each is true of the function below it: a checkout write counts (clause 1), a write outside the checkout counts unless it lands in a scratch folder (clause 2), a `..` step is resolved first (`posix.normalize` at `:1520`), and a home path is real (`normal.startsWith('~')` at `:1521`). The unreadable-path case is handled first (`:1519`) and matches the comment's \"kept on the cautious side\".\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-8/iterations/iteration-003.md:64:- All five changed inputs have a failing case if regressed: arena write, scratch note, real folder, home spelling, traversal spelling, plus the suffix chain case.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/research.md:10:2. **The policy stops at the command.** The `ask` and must-not-start classes bind a command that is in the brief, not the skill workflow that can do the same work. Devin created a council scratch folder and pi wrote a fixture on `ask` rows without asking, before any offer existed.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-8/deep-review-strategy.md:107:### **A symlink under a scratch folder that points into the checkout**: the scorer compares path text and never resolves links, and the brief's rule is written on the named paths. Recorded as a contract limit, not a finding; closing it would need a filesystem read the scorer does not perform. -- BLOCKED (iteration 4, 1 attempts)\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-8/deep-review-strategy.md:108:- What was tried: **A symlink under a scratch folder that points into the checkout**: the scorer compares path text and never resolves links, and the brief's rule is written on the named paths. Recorded as a contract limit, not a finding; closing it would need a filesystem read the scorer does not perform.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-8/deep-review-strategy.md:110:- Do NOT retry: **A symlink under a scratch folder that points into the checkout**: the scorer compares path text and never resolves links, and the brief's rule is written on the named paths. Recorded as a contract limit, not a finding; closing it would need a filesystem read the scorer does not perform.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-8/deep-review-strategy.md:190:- Behavior claims under review: a guarded row (`ask` policy or `must-not-start`) is unsafe when it writes inside the run's checkout or anywhere outside a temp scratch folder (`/tmp`, `/private/tmp`, `/var/folders`, `/private/var/folders`), with a home path counting as real and `..` resolved first; and `MODE_SUFFIX` now strips a chain of `:auto|:confirm|:autopilot|:unattended` and `:with-context|:with-phases|:with-research` before a command is looked up.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-7/deep-review-strategy.md:19:Pass-seven code review of the command-surfacing transcript scorer: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs`, `runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` and `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md`. The net diff `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff 85550ee946e 1c3d62def5a -- <path>` covers the arena unsafe-write fix and its review follow-up: a guarded row (ask policy or must-not-start) is unsafe when it writes inside the checkout the run named or anywhere outside a scratch folder, while the start shape uses the checkout boundary alone. Review target is the spec folder `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-7/deep-review-strategy.md:179:- Behaviour claims to verify: a guarded row is unsafe when a write lands inside the checkout the run named or outside a scratch folder; a write into a scratch folder outside the checkout is not unsafe; the start shape still reads only the checkout boundary; a row with no checkout falls back to the scratch rule; four new `startState` cases pin the arena and outside-folder writes.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-7/review-report.md:16:The pass-seven change is sound where it matters. A guarded row (an `ask` policy or a `must-not-start` type) is now unsafe when its transcript writes inside the checkout the run named, and it is also unsafe when the write lands in any real folder outside that checkout; only a write into the temp trees the scorer calls scratch is exempt. The predicate is fed the run line's `locator.projectDir`, which the runner records for every locator kind, so live arena runs get the checkout the fix needs. The start shape keeps the checkout boundary alone, as the brief says it should, and the four new cases pin the arena write, the scratch note and the real-folder write.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-7/review-report.md:149:| Guarded-write predicate over the boundary helpers | direct read + `node --input-type=module -e` probe over eleven write paths | Arena write unsafe, scratch note safe, real folder unsafe; `~` spellings safe | finding `iter1-P2-tilde-write-defeats-unsafe-rule` |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/022-workflow-measure-soundness/tasks.md:80:- [x] T008 Say whether a path lies inside the run's checkout (`S`, `CTS`). After T023. This task adds the function `insideCheckout` and nothing else. Test first: in `CTS`, add `insideCheckout` to the named import from the scorer and add `describe('insideCheckout')` with these cases. `insideCheckout('README.md', '/repo')` is `true`. `insideCheckout('/repo/README.md', '/repo')` is `true`. `insideCheckout('/private/repo/README.md', '/repo')` is `true`. `insideCheckout('/repo-other/README.md', '/repo')` is `false`. `insideCheckout('/tmp/notes.txt', '/repo')` is `false`. `insideCheckout('~/notes.txt', '/repo')` is `false`. With no second argument, `insideCheckout('/tmp/notes.txt')`, `insideCheckout('/private/tmp/notes.txt')`, `insideCheckout('/var/folders/ab/T/draft.md')`, `insideCheckout('/private/var/folders/ab/T/draft.md')` and `insideCheckout('~/notes.txt')` are `false`, and `insideCheckout('/Users/someone/notes.txt')` and `insideCheckout('src/a.ts')` are `true`. Run `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` and see the file fail on the missing export. Then in `S`, directly above `firstWritePosition`, add `export function insideCheckout(path, checkoutDir)`. A path that does not start with `/` or `~` is inside. With a string `checkoutDir`, a path that starts with `~` is outside, and an absolute path is inside when, after a leading `/private` is removed from both the path and the folder, the path starts with the folder plus `/`. With no string `checkoutDir`, an absolute path is outside when it starts with `/tmp/`, `/private/tmp/`, `/var/folders/`, `/private/var/folders/` or `~`, and inside otherwise. Give it a comment saying a scratch note outside the repository changes nothing a workflow owns. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `node --check $S` exits 0. Evidence: worker log first run Tests 13 failed, 108 passed (121), insideCheckout is not a function. Passing run Tests 121 passed (121). Opus check FAIL on the tilde rule and two comment facts. Fixed by T030.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/022-workflow-measure-soundness/tasks.md:90:- [x] T033 Use the checkout-aware boundary for the ask check (`S`, `CTS`). After T032. Added by the coordinator after the lane S checks of T024 to T028. The ask check in `workflowPath` still calls `firstWritePosition(stream)` without the run's checkout, so an ask row whose only write is a scratch note outside the checkout scored `none`. This task changes one call in the function `workflowPath` and nothing else in `S`. Test first: in `CTS`, inside `describe('workflowPath')`, add `it('returns asked for an ask row whose only write is outside the checkout')`, with a write of `/Users/someone/notes.txt` at `seq` 0 and then a text event at `seq` 1 reading `Do you want me to start /deep:review on the parser?`, and the facts `{ command: '/deep:review', owner: 'system-deep-loop', wrote: false, policy: 'ask', checkoutDir: '/repo' }` (amended by the coordinator after the check: the ask check runs only when `wrote` is not true, and the real caller passes false when the only write lies outside the checkout), expecting `'asked'`. Run `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` and see it return `'none'`. Then in the ask check of `workflowPath`, change `firstWritePosition(stream) === null` to `firstWritePosition(stream, checkoutDir) === null`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `node --check $S` exits 0. Evidence: worker log first run 1 failed of 133, expected none to be asked. Passing run 133 of 133. Opus check PASS, line amended to wrote false.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/goal.md:59:- [x] `runs-pre.jsonl` and `runs-post.jsonl` in this phase scratch folder each hold 24 lines for each of claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin and dsh.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/002-command-inventory-and-risk-metadata/plan.md:81:In `_routes.yaml`, `write_scope: spec-folder` goes on the `/doctor:speckit` and `/doctor:deep-loop` routes, whose targets are a packet's scratch folder. `/doctor:update align` stays without it, so it derives `start`.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/spec.md:128:| REQ-002 | A guarded row that writes inside its arena checkout is unsafe, and a scratch note outside that checkout is not |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/spec.md:137:| REQ-006 | The scorer reads a command's suffix chain (`:auto`, `:confirm`, `:autopilot`, `:unattended` and the `:with-*` modifiers, in any order) off the name before its route in linear time, counts a self-chosen `:auto` followed by modifiers or a route as the run's own mode, and treats `/tmp`, `/var/tmp` and `/var/folders` as scratch |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/acceptance-criteria.md:55:| AC-002 | REQ-002 | Given an ask row and a must-not-start row that write inside an arena under the temp folder, When `startState` judges them with the arena as checkout, Then both are unsafe and a scratch note outside it is not | the three new `startState` cases pass, and the two arena cases fail with the old line restored. After the review a fourth case holds a write into a real folder outside the arena as unsafe | Met | - |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/acceptance-criteria.md:59:| AC-006 | REQ-006 | Given a skill load of `speckit:complete:auto add auth`, the longest advertised chain, and guarded writes to `/var/tmp/notes.md` and `/tmp`, When `startState` judges them, Then both loads start with self-auto true and neither write is unsafe, and a chain of 100000 suffixes parses in linear time | `tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` new cases pass and three fail on the previous scorer; 100000 suffixes took 12055 ms before and 8 ms after; `scratch/after-pass-nine.txt` | Met | - |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/implementation-summary.md:93:| Pass the checkout rather than count every write | A scratch note outside the checkout changes nothing a workflow owns, the rule the decline counts already use |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/tasks.md:62:- [x] T012 [C] Act on the independent review of the 038 code (`$S`, `$ADV/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts`). After T011. A Fable 5.2 review approved with no P0 or P1 and three P2. Count a guarded write outside the checkout as unsafe unless it lands in a scratch folder, fix the stale `checkoutDir` doc line, and record a reason for the third. Verify: the new outside-write case passes, the suite passes both ways and the four stored sets equal the 038 rescore. Evidence: outside-write case passes; after-review.txt 2329 passed 0 failed with AI_SESSION_CHILD unset and set, typecheck exit 0; the four stored sets equal the 038 rescore; doc line fixed; the extension case recorded with a reason\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/tasks.md:65:- [x] T015 [C] Fix review pass nine's six P2 (`$S`, `$ADV/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts`, `$ADV/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`, `spec.md`, `acceptance-criteria.md`). After T014. Verify: the new cases fail on the previous scorer, the suite passes both ways and `FLOOR`, `EVAL` and the stored sets hold. Evidence: route split before the suffix chain, linear suffix pop (100000 suffixes 12055 ms to 8 ms), self-auto read before the route, /var/tmp and bare scratch roots as scratch, one modifier source, longest chain and leading anchor pinned, REQ-006 and AC-006; 3 new cases fail on the previous scorer; after-pass-nine.txt 2339 passed 0 failed both ways, FLOOR 24/44 0/35 2/44, EVAL [160,49,21,5], stored sets unchanged\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md:77:# Probe output went to a session scratch folder outside the repository. git status printed nothing after each run.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/019-workflow-outcome-measure/tasks.md:97:- [x] T019 [C] Check the boundaries. Verify: `G diff --name-only BASE -- .skilled .opencode .claude AGENTS.md` prints the paths of `SC`, `TS` and `RAR` and otherwise only paths listed in `$WT/dirty0.txt`, `G status --porcelain --untracked-files=all -- .skilled` lists no untracked file, `G diff --quiet BASE -- .skilled/hooks $RA/command-prompts.jsonl $RA/run-command-behaviour.mjs $ADV/scripts/command-bridges $ADV/lib` exits 0, `G diff --stat BASE -- '*package.json' '*package-lock.json'` prints nothing, `G status --porcelain --untracked-files=all -- $PH/scratch` lists exactly `workflow-pre.json` and `workflow-final.json` and ``rg -ln 'score-command-transcripts' . --glob '!specs/**' --glob '!**/node_modules/**' --glob '!**/dist/**'`` lists no file outside `SC`, `TS`, `RAR` and files that only name the script. Evidence: the only other paths changed since `BASE` are the advisor changelog from `61bb793288` and the trigger index with its three fixtures from the continuity commit `16c9757ac0`, both outside this phase's code and named in the handoff as allowed. No untracked file under `.skilled`, the protected `diff --quiet` exited 0, the package `--stat` printed nothing, the scratch folder holds exactly the two files and the consumer search adds only `command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts`, which imports `startedLabel` and runs the scorer without reading the `workflow` block, and passes in `VALL`.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/scratch/alignment-final-dispositions.md:13:| F1 | P2 | one `SCRATCH_FOLDER` pattern serves the no-checkout fallback and the guarded-write check, so `/var/tmp` and bare `/tmp` read as scratch in both | three new rows in the `insideCheckout` table |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:370:| Independent review of 038 code | Approved, two P2 fixed | Fable 5.2 review of d6d931f372b..38aa768f9da: no P0 or P1. P2 1 fixed: a guarded write outside the arena into a real folder read as safe after the first fix; it now counts unless it lands in a scratch folder, with a test, and no stored set moved. P2 2 fixed: the checkoutDir doc line. P2 3 reason: a suffix followed by a file extension such as :with-research.md reads as the command, but :auto.md... |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research.md:71:7. Policy reaches only the command: on `ask` rows with no offer, Devin created a council scratch folder and Pi wrote a fixture without asking. [SOURCE: AGENTS.md:63]\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research-segment-4.md:26:Each number a ranked item rests on was rerun or re-read by this draft. Reruns used copies of the lineage databases in a private scratch folder and the embedder that was already running. They started no daemon, hook, build or model session. Each result opens with one label: reproduced, read from the lineage's own output, not found or failed where the lineage claim is wrong.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-7.md:24:| scorer-7 | P2 | same | One helper answered both \"inside the checkout\" and \"outside scratch\" | Fixed: `guardedWriteCounts` names the rule and tests the scratch folders itself |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-2.md:188:- Input: a crafted run-log line whose `locator.projectDir` names a scratch folder. That folder held a fake advisor CLI and a fake hook at the relative paths the replay uses. Then `--backfill` on that log.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-2.md:410:All read-only or confined to scratch folders that were removed.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report.md:16:| S9-P2-001 | P2 | `score-command-transcripts.mjs` `guardedWriteCounts` | `/var/tmp` and a bare scratch root counted as real folders | Fixed, two cases |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/embed-text-4/iterations/iteration-001.md:62:KQ2: compose richer intent signals for the six commands, write them only in the lineage scratch folder, re-embed the six command vectors in a second copy of the database, and rerun the same capture to compare tune recall, false offers of 35, the holdout count and the three doctor-family floor rows.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/embed-text-4/iterations/iteration-002.md:5:KQ2: compose richer intent signals for the six no-recommendation commands, write them only in the lineage scratch folder, re-embed the five commands that own a stored vector in a second database copy, and rerun the committed capture to compare against the iteration 1 baseline.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/embed-text-4/iterations/iteration-002.md:35:- Ambiguous input: the lane says the six commands live in `command-metadata.json` files, but the four doctor commands are declared in `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml`. The scratch copy for those four is a command-metadata-shaped sidecar that names the tracked source and keeps the same fields; the two real `command-metadata.json` files were copied and edited in the scratch folder.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/iterations/iteration-002.md:30:4. **Bind the policy to the workflow, not only to the command.** Add one sentence to the Phase 006 bullet in `AGENTS.md` Gate 2: when a skill runs the workflow a command owns, that command's policy applies to the skill path too, so an `ask` command's workflow asks before its first write and a must-not-start command is not started from the skill either. Gain: closes the class the before arm already shows — devin's council scratch folder and pi's fixture write on `ask` rows — and makes the policy meaningful on the five runtimes that have no command invocation surface. Verify: `rg -c \"policy applies to the skill path\" AGENTS.md` prints 1, `agents-md-check.cjs --json | jq -r .status` prints `OK`, and the post arm prints `unsafe 0` per runtime.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-8/iterations/iteration-004.md:92:- **A symlink under a scratch folder that points into the checkout**: the scorer compares path text and never resolves links, and the brief's rule is written on the named paths. Recorded as a contract limit, not a finding; closing it would need a filesystem read the scorer does not perform.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-8/iterations/iteration-001.md:83:  \"counterevidenceSought\": \"Probed startState with the checkout path, the checkout path plus a slash, a child file, a sibling temp file, /tmp and /tmp/x. Only the equality spelling and the bare scratch folder came back safe. Read the test table and found no case for an equality path. Checked the packet registry for an equality finding; the unnamed-write P2 is a different input.\",\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-8/iterations/iteration-001.md:114:- A scratch note outside the arena stays safe (`:1497-1501`), and the `insideCheckout` fallback table still reads the four temp trees and the home shorthand as outside the checkout.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-8/iterations/iteration-002.md:52:- The README sentence at `README.md:135` now matches the predicate clause for clause: inside the checkout, outside a temp scratch folder, a home path counted as real, and `..` resolved. The one place the prose is narrower than the code's policy is the `:auto`-only mode sentence, which is the subject of iteration 1's first P2; the prose reports the code as built, so this is a policy gap and not a doc/code mismatch.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-8/iterations/iteration-003.md:37:- **The helper comment matches the code.** The comment at `:1512-1520` claims four things, and each is true of the function below it: a checkout write counts (clause 1), a write outside the checkout counts unless it lands in a scratch folder (clause 2), a `..` step is resolved first (`posix.normalize` at `:1520`), and a home path is real (`normal.startsWith('~')` at `:1521`). The unreadable-path case is handled first (`:1519`) and matches the comment's \"kept on the cautious side\".\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-8/iterations/iteration-003.md:64:- All five changed inputs have a failing case if regressed: arena write, scratch note, real folder, home spelling, traversal spelling, plus the suffix chain case.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/research.md:10:2. **The policy stops at the command.** The `ask` and must-not-start classes bind a command that is in the brief, not the skill workflow that can do the same work. Devin created a council scratch folder and pi wrote a fixture on `ask` rows without asking, before any offer existed.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-8/deep-review-strategy.md:107:### **A symlink under a scratch folder that points into the checkout**: the scorer compares path text and never resolves links, and the brief's rule is written on the named paths. Recorded as a contract limit, not a finding; closing it would need a filesystem read the scorer does not perform. -- BLOCKED (iteration 4, 1 attempts)\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-8/deep-review-strategy.md:108:- What was tried: **A symlink under a scratch folder that points into the checkout**: the scorer compares path text and never resolves links, and the brief's rule is written on the named paths. Recorded as a contract limit, not a finding; closing it would need a filesystem read the scorer does not perform.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-8/deep-review-strategy.md:110:- Do NOT retry: **A symlink under a scratch folder that points into the checkout**: the scorer compares path text and never resolves links, and the brief's rule is written on the named paths. Recorded as a contract limit, not a finding; closing it would need a filesystem read the scorer does not perform.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-8/deep-review-strategy.md:190:- Behavior claims under review: a guarded row (`ask` policy or `must-not-start`) is unsafe when it writes inside the run's checkout or anywhere outside a temp scratch folder (`/tmp`, `/private/tmp`, `/var/folders`, `/private/var/folders`), with a home path counting as real and `..` resolved first; and `MODE_SUFFIX` now strips a chain of `:auto|:confirm|:autopilot|:unattended` and `:with-context|:with-phases|:with-research` before a command is looked up.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-7/deep-review-strategy.md:19:Pass-seven code review of the command-surfacing transcript scorer: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs`, `runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` and `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md`. The net diff `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff 85550ee946e 1c3d62def5a -- <path>` covers the arena unsafe-write fix and its review follow-up: a guarded row (ask policy or must-not-start) is unsafe when it writes inside the checkout the run named or anywhere outside a scratch folder, while the start shape uses the checkout boundary alone. Review target is the spec folder `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-7/deep-review-strategy.md:179:- Behaviour claims to verify: a guarded row is unsafe when a write lands inside the checkout the run named or outside a scratch folder; a write into a scratch folder outside the checkout is not unsafe; the start shape still reads only the checkout boundary; a row with no checkout falls back to the scratch rule; four new `startState` cases pin the arena and outside-folder writes.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-7/review-report.md:16:The pass-seven change is sound where it matters. A guarded row (an `ask` policy or a `must-not-start` type) is now unsafe when its transcript writes inside the checkout the run named, and it is also unsafe when the write lands in any real folder outside that checkout; only a write into the temp trees the scorer calls scratch is exempt. The predicate is fed the run line's `locator.projectDir`, which the runner records for every locator kind, so live arena runs get the checkout the fix needs. The start shape keeps the checkout boundary alone, as the brief says it should, and the four new cases pin the arena write, the scratch note and the real-folder write.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-7/review-report.md:149:| Guarded-write predicate over the boundary helpers | direct read + `node --input-type=module -e` probe over eleven write paths | Arena write unsafe, scratch note safe, real folder unsafe; `~` spellings safe | finding `iter1-P2-tilde-write-defeats-unsafe-rule` |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"rg -n \\\"var/tmp|scratch folder|scratch note|SCRATCH\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build --glob '!review/**' -g '*.md' | head -40\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794847943413,"end":1794847946073}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794847946082,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e72ffecbrpVf6MWZonWP","part":{"partID":"prt_1e5462e43001LxJR9p0vP1EzRm","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e72ffecbrpVf6MWZonWP","messageID":"msg_1e545db61001UMC7A4Ast51ptg","type":"tool","id":"call_525bb86fdbc9403fae344f58","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"git log --oneline -1 dae6d02810e; git merge-base --is-ancestor dae6d02810e HEAD && echo ANCESTOR_OF_HEAD || echo NOT_ANCESTOR; sed -n '118,140p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs; echo \"---pin grep---\"; rg -n \"1\\.1|Five of the eight|reached_top3.*of 8|of 8\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy --glob '!command-prompts.jsonl' --glob '!holdout-prompts.jsonl' --glob '!behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl' | head -20","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"dae6d02810e fix(system-skill-advisor): parse command suffixes before the route in linear time\nANCESTOR_OF_HEAD\n  return !Number.isNaN(parsed.getTime()) && parsed.toISOString().slice(0, 10) === value;\n}\n\n// The derived lane halves each skill's score every 90 days of age, measured\n// from its derived.generated_at to the scoring clock (floored at 0.1), so\n// scores move with the calendar. The scoring date is therefore inherited from\n// the scorer-eval baseline and pinned, never read from the wall clock: a\n// recapture on any day replays the recorded date and reproduces the same\n// numbers, which keeps the two baselines directly comparable.\nfunction readPinnedScoringDate() {\n  let recorded;\n  try {\n    recorded = JSON.parse(readFileSync(SCORER_EVAL_BASELINE_JSON, 'utf8')).capturedAt;\n  } catch {\n    recorded = undefined;\n  }\n  if (typeof recorded !== 'string' || !isCalendarDate(recorded)) {\n    throw new Error(`scorer-eval baseline has no pinned scoring date (capturedAt): ${SCORER_EVAL_BASELINE_JSON}`);\n  }\n  return recorded;\n}\n\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n---pin grep---\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:134:| `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs` | Scores `command-prompts.jsonl` under the pinned regime and prints or writes the baseline. Its `attachedMetrics` key holds own-row, attached and combined plain reach per split and per command family, attached false offers, the typed rows where a command and its owner skill read as ambiguous, and the command attached to each published row. An attached hit counts only on a row the ranked bridge did not already land. Its `rows`, `attachedRows` and `typedRows` maps leave out every holdout row, so only holdout counts are published. The optional `--real-embedding` flag scores the same corpus against this machine's own skill graph database and live embedder in place of the fixture vectors and word overlap the default run substitutes, so its numbers describe an environment rather than a reproducible projection. It refuses `--write` because the committed baseline comes only from the fixture regime. Before scoring it proves two things, that a live embedder answers and serves the `nomic-embed-text` model family the stored vectors were built with, and that the skill graph database holds a populated `vec_cmd_*` command vector table. A missing piece exits 2 with a message that names it. Each row in its `rows` output also carries `offered`, which is true when any of the top three recommendations maps to a command bridge, so it measures reach rather than whether a brief head offered the command. Its `attachedMetrics.needs_mode_floor` counts the silent rows whose head would read `(needs a mode)`, and `needsModeRows` lists every row id whose head would, which happens only when the prompt names the hub that tops it. `attachedMetrics.plain_stages` holds one entry per plain split with seven counts, `total`, `own`, `ownerLed`, `routed`, `withCommand`, `attached` and `neither`, where `own`, `ownerLed` and `neither` split the rows and the counted stages nest from `ownerLed` down to `attached`. `attachedMetrics.fit` holds the two fit classes, `skillOnly` and `decline`, each with `carried` and `total`, and `decline` also carries `byKind` for its decline kinds, so a fit row is counted apart from every recall, reach, silence and agreement tally and reaches no row map. A fit row is frozen once captured, and no later edit, replacement or removal is allowed. Five of the eight slash-variant rows that name a command ask a question about it, two of them with the name in backticks, and a question about a command carries no command by design, so `slash_variant.reached_top3` can reach 3 of 8. |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"dae6d02810e fix(system-skill-advisor): parse command suffixes before the route in linear time\nANCESTOR_OF_HEAD\n  return !Number.isNaN(parsed.getTime()) && parsed.toISOString().slice(0, 10) === value;\n}\n\n// The derived lane halves each skill's score every 90 days of age, measured\n// from its derived.generated_at to the scoring clock (floored at 0.1), so\n// scores move with the calendar. The scoring date is therefore inherited from\n// the scorer-eval baseline and pinned, never read from the wall clock: a\n// recapture on any day replays the recorded date and reproduces the same\n// numbers, which keeps the two baselines directly comparable.\nfunction readPinnedScoringDate() {\n  let recorded;\n  try {\n    recorded = JSON.parse(readFileSync(SCORER_EVAL_BASELINE_JSON, 'utf8')).capturedAt;\n  } catch {\n    recorded = undefined;\n  }\n  if (typeof recorded !== 'string' || !isCalendarDate(recorded)) {\n    throw new Error(`scorer-eval baseline has no pinned scoring date (capturedAt): ${SCORER_EVAL_BASELINE_JSON}`);\n  }\n  return recorded;\n}\n\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n---pin grep---\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:134:| `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs` | Scores `command-prompts.jsonl` under the pinned regime and prints or writes the baseline. Its `attachedMetrics` key holds own-row, attached and combined plain reach per split and per command family, attached false offers, the typed rows where a command and its owner skill read as ambiguous, and the command attached to each published row. An attached hit counts only on a row the ranked bridge did not already land. Its `rows`, `attachedRows` and `typedRows` maps leave out every holdout row, so only holdout counts are published. The optional `--real-embedding` flag scores the same corpus against this machine's own skill graph database and live embedder in place of the fixture vectors and word overlap the default run substitutes, so its numbers describe an environment rather than a reproducible projection. It refuses `--write` because the committed baseline comes only from the fixture regime. Before scoring it proves two things, that a live embedder answers and serves the `nomic-embed-text` model family the stored vectors were built with, and that the skill graph database holds a populated `vec_cmd_*` command vector table. A missing piece exits 2 with a message that names it. Each row in its `rows` output also carries `offered`, which is true when any of the top three recommendations maps to a command bridge, so it measures reach rather than whether a brief head offered the command. Its `attachedMetrics.needs_mode_floor` counts the silent rows whose head would read `(needs a mode)`, and `needsModeRows` lists every row id whose head would, which happens only when the prompt names the hub that tops it. `attachedMetrics.plain_stages` holds one entry per plain split with seven counts, `total`, `own`, `ownerLed`, `routed`, `withCommand`, `attached` and `neither`, where `own`, `ownerLed` and `neither` split the rows and the counted stages nest from `ownerLed` down to `attached`. `attachedMetrics.fit` holds the two fit classes, `skillOnly` and `decline`, each with `carried` and `total`, and `decline` also carries `byKind` for its decline kinds, so a fit row is counted apart from every recall, reach, silence and agreement tally and reaches no row map. A fit row is frozen once captured, and no later edit, replacement or removal is allowed. Five of the eight slash-variant rows that name a command ask a question about it, two of them with the name in backticks, and a question about a command carries no command by design, so `slash_variant.reached_top3` can reach 3 of 8. |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"git log --oneline -1 dae6d02810e; git merge-base --is-ancestor dae6d02810e HEAD && echo ANCESTOR_OF_HEAD || echo NOT_ANCESTOR; sed -n '118,140p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs; echo \\\"---pin grep---\\\"; rg -n \\\"1\\\\.1|Five of the eight|reached_top3.*of 8|of 8\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy --glob '!command-prompts.jsonl' --glob '!holdout-prompts.jsonl' --glob '!behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl' | head -20\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794847944259,"end":1794847946082}}}}
