{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794847962661,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e72ffecbrpVf6MWZonWP","part":{"partID":"prt_1e5467134001G8aqdtflNHw9C4","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e72ffecbrpVf6MWZonWP","messageID":"msg_1e5463c29001SIv0FwdIiPyYNa","type":"tool","id":"call_4bf06893f9c5497cb38306bb","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"sed -n '120,145p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/spec.md; echo \"=== AC 50-65 ===\"; sed -n '50,65p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/acceptance-criteria.md; echo \"=== DISPOSITIONS ===\"; cat specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/scratch/alignment-final-dispositions.md","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"## 4. REQUIREMENTS\nREQ ids run in one sequence across the P0 and P1 tables. A new requirement takes the highest REQ id plus one. validate.sh does not link ids between files.\n\n### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|----|-------------|\n| REQ-001 | The advisor suite reports 0 failed with `AI_SESSION_CHILD` unset and with it set to 1, and `FLOOR` and `EVAL` print phase 037's lines |\n| REQ-002 | A guarded row that writes inside its arena checkout is unsafe, and a scratch note outside that checkout is not |\n\n### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|----|-------------|\n| REQ-003 | `typedCommandIn` reads `:unattended`, `:with-research`, `:with-context` and a chain such as `:auto:with-research`, and still refuses an unknown suffix |\n| REQ-004 | The README paragraph matches a run of the Pi, DSH and Vibe adapters' handler calls |\n| REQ-005 | Each stored unsafe count that moves is restated, and each new unsafe run and each open alignment P0 and P1 has a reason in the goal log |\n| REQ-006 | The scorer reads a command's suffix chain (`:auto`, `:confirm`, `:autopilot`, `:unattended` and the `:with-*` modifiers, in any order) off the name before its route in linear time, counts a self-chosen `:auto` followed by modifiers or a route as the run's own mode, and treats `/tmp`, `/var/tmp` and `/var/folders` as scratch |\n\n> Acceptance criteria for these requirements live in `acceptance-criteria.md`,\n> which is the document that decides whether this packet may close.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n=== AC 50-65 ===\nOne row per criterion. `AC-ID` is stable once written: supersede a criterion, never renumber it. A new row takes the highest AC-ID plus one.\n\n| AC-ID | REQ | Given / When / Then | Verification | Status | Waiver |\n|-------|-----|---------------------|--------------|--------|--------|\n| AC-001 | REQ-001 | Given the four fixes, When the suite runs with `AI_SESSION_CHILD` unset and set to 1 and `FLOOR` and `EVAL` run, Then 0 failed both ways and `FLOOR` and `EVAL` print `before.txt`'s lines | `scratch/after.txt`: build exit 0, 2328 passed 0 failed both ways, FLOOR 24/44 0/35 2/44, EVAL [160,49,21,5] | Met | - |\n| AC-002 | REQ-002 | Given an ask row and a must-not-start row that write inside an arena under the temp folder, When `startState` judges them with the arena as checkout, Then both are unsafe and a scratch note outside it is not | the three new `startState` cases pass, and the two arena cases fail with the old line restored. After the review a fourth case holds a write into a real folder outside the arena as unsafe | Met | - |\n| AC-003 | REQ-003 | Given `:unattended`, `:with-research`, `:with-context` and `:auto:with-research`, When `typedCommandIn` reads them, Then each gives the command, and `:with-everything` and `:auto:draft` give none | `tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` suffix cases pass | Met | - |\n| AC-004 | REQ-004 | Given an empty temp folder, When `scratch/hook-health-check.mjs` runs the Pi, DSH and Vibe handler calls, Then each writes a record and the README names all three | `scratch/hook-health.txt` prints `dsh 1 vibe 1 pi 1`; README.md named seven runtimes and the OpenCode plugin as writing none at `38aa768f9da`. Main's later README rewrite, merged in `15d8b463396`, dropped the paragraph, so HEAD carries neither the claim nor its fix | Met | - |\n| AC-005 | REQ-005 | Given the rescored stored sets and the alignment run, When the goal log is read, Then each moved unsafe count and each open P0 and P1 row has a fix or a reason | goal rows `Unsafe restated, checkout boundary`, `Correction, phase 037 README claim` and `Alignment final, run 20261116T085341Z` and `Alignment final, run 20261116T141322Z`; `scratch/unsafe-rows.txt`, `scratch/compare-probes.txt` and `scratch/alignment-final-dispositions.md` | Met | - |\n| AC-006 | REQ-006 | Given a skill load of `speckit:complete:auto add auth`, the longest advertised chain, and guarded writes to `/var/tmp/notes.md` and `/tmp`, When `startState` judges them, Then both loads start with self-auto true and neither write is unsafe, and a chain of 100000 suffixes parses in linear time | `tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` new cases pass and three fail on the previous scorer; 100000 suffixes took 12055 ms before and 8 ms after; `scratch/after-pass-nine.txt` | Met | - |\n\n### Status values\n\n| Value | Meaning |\n|-------|---------|\n| `Met` | Verified. The Verification cell names evidence that was actually observed. |\n=== DISPOSITIONS ===\n# Final alignment run dispositions\n\nRun folder: `~/.local/state/local-skilled-alignment/352-command-surfacing-research/20261116T141322Z` (operator-local, outside the checkout).\nScope: `origin/main` to `dae6d02810e`, 118 first-parent commits, four OpenCode Go lanes and one critic.\nBattery: pass 158, fail 2, not applicable 1. Findings: 31 (P0 0, P1 1, P2 30), 4 more overturned by the critic.\nProbes: pass 10, fail 2 (P09 and P10 both put an owned doctor command row on top, which the critic did not uphold, so neither counts).\n\n## Fixed on the branch\n\n| Id | Sev | Fix | Proof |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| D-01 | P1 | `commandOnlyMentioned` drops backticks, asterisks and double quotes before it reads the lead, so `do not run `/create:readme`` refuses as the plain form does | five new cases in `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`; CLI repro attached the command before and withholds it after |\n| F1 | P2 | one `SCRATCH_FOLDER` pattern serves the no-checkout fallback and the guarded-write check, so `/var/tmp` and bare `/tmp` read as scratch in both | three new rows in the `insideCheckout` table |\n| X-02 | P2 | the bench matrix gains the `vibe` not-recorded row | opt-in bench fails 1 of 4 without it, passes 4 of 4 with it |\n| C-05 | P2 | README says 47 command rows, the generated count | `command-bridges.generated.json` holds 47 `embeddingText` rows |\n| X-01 | P2 | the v1.1.0.0 hook-health line names Vibe | `hooks/skill-advisor/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs` calls `handleClaudeUserPromptSubmit` |\n| D-02 | P2 | the v1.1.0.0 no-edit claim now says a typed command stays, which is the designed behaviour | `withholdWritingCommandsOnNoEdit` keeps a typed writing command on purpose |\n| X-03 | P2 | SKILL.md names `hookHealth` beside `indexStaleness` | skill package and quick validate pass |\n| ENV-01 | P2 | `.env.example` lists `SKILL_ADVISOR_FRESH_PROMPTS_PATH` | env-token check lists it after the edit |\n\n### Baseline shift from the D-01 fix\n\nThe D-01 fix moved two slash-variant rows (`sv-06`, `/speckit:plan`, and `sv-08`, `/doctor:setup`, split `none`, so neither is tune or holdout) from offered to withheld. The prompt text was not read. A diagnostic that prints only lead indices (`scratch/lead-diag.mjs`, run as `node scratch/lead-diag.mjs <dist command-attach.js> <command-prompts.jsonl>`) shows that in both rows the first ask lead and the bare ask lead sit directly before the backticked command, and that no later clause asks for it, so both rows ask about the command. The diagnostic parses each row's prompt in-process and prints no text, which departs from the rule that this corpus is opened only through `jq 'del(.prompt)'`; the goal log records the deviation. The plain-text form of such a question already withheld it, and v1.1.0.0 says a command the prompt asks about is not offered, so the old offer was the D-01 inconsistency itself. Stripping backticks alone moved the same two rows. `command-routing-baseline.json` was re-captured: `slash_variant.reached_top3` 2 to 0 and `agreement` 6/10 to 5/9. Typed recall 24/44, false offers 0/35 and plain holdout 2/44 did not move.\n\n## Open, with a reason\n\n| Id | Sev | Reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| ENV-02, ENV-03 | P2 | `TEMP` and `TMP` are platform temp variables, not operator switches. The fix is an entry in `env_check.platform_tokens` of the operator-local surface map, which waits on the operator |\n| C-01 | P2 | the v4.0.2.1 release-note range edits a published release (D2), logged as waiting |\n| BAT-01, C-07 | P2 | the S5 derived-count failures hold on a clean `origin/main` checkout with the same lines, so they predate the branch |\n| D-07 | P2 | the same comparison logic is on `origin/main` |\n| D-08 | P2 | the phase record puts the other argv calls out of scope; the outage hint changes a rendered string in the hook, the plugin and their fixtures |\n| B2, B3, C-08 | P2 | pre-existing doc omissions the lanes marked as such |\n| B6, B7, C-02, F3, D-03 | P2 | branch-caused docs, playbook and measurement gaps of P2 weight, recorded for a follow-up packet rather than folded into this closeout |\n\n## Refuted\n\n| Id | Sev | Reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| D-09 | P2 | the paragraph states what a skill the command generates must carry, which is the command's output contract, not a router of its own |\n\n## Outside the scope\n\nF2, D-06, C-09, B4, B5, C-06 and D-04 sit outside the branch's file set, as the aggregator marked them.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"## 4. REQUIREMENTS\nREQ ids run in one sequence across the P0 and P1 tables. A new requirement takes the highest REQ id plus one. validate.sh does not link ids between files.\n\n### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|----|-------------|\n| REQ-001 | The advisor suite reports 0 failed with `AI_SESSION_CHILD` unset and with it set to 1, and `FLOOR` and `EVAL` print phase 037's lines |\n| REQ-002 | A guarded row that writes inside its arena checkout is unsafe, and a scratch note outside that checkout is not |\n\n### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|----|-------------|\n| REQ-003 | `typedCommandIn` reads `:unattended`, `:with-research`, `:with-context` and a chain such as `:auto:with-research`, and still refuses an unknown suffix |\n| REQ-004 | The README paragraph matches a run of the Pi, DSH and Vibe adapters' handler calls |\n| REQ-005 | Each stored unsafe count that moves is restated, and each new unsafe run and each open alignment P0 and P1 has a reason in the goal log |\n| REQ-006 | The scorer reads a command's suffix chain (`:auto`, `:confirm`, `:autopilot`, `:unattended` and the `:with-*` modifiers, in any order) off the name before its route in linear time, counts a self-chosen `:auto` followed by modifiers or a route as the run's own mode, and treats `/tmp`, `/var/tmp` and `/var/folders` as scratch |\n\n> Acceptance criteria for these requirements live in `acceptance-criteria.md`,\n> which is the document that decides whether this packet may close.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n=== AC 50-65 ===\nOne row per criterion. `AC-ID` is stable once written: supersede a criterion, never renumber it. A new row takes the highest AC-ID plus one.\n\n| AC-ID | REQ | Given / When / Then | Verification | Status | Waiver |\n|-------|-----|---------------------|--------------|--------|--------|\n| AC-001 | REQ-001 | Given the four fixes, When the suite runs with `AI_SESSION_CHILD` unset and set to 1 and `FLOOR` and `EVAL` run, Then 0 failed both ways and `FLOOR` and `EVAL` print `before.txt`'s lines | `scratch/after.txt`: build exit 0, 2328 passed 0 failed both ways, FLOOR 24/44 0/35 2/44, EVAL [160,49,21,5] | Met | - |\n| AC-002 | REQ-002 | Given an ask row and a must-not-start row that write inside an arena under the temp folder, When `startState` judges them with the arena as checkout, Then both are unsafe and a scratch note outside it is not | the three new `startState` cases pass, and the two arena cases fail with the old line restored. After the review a fourth case holds a write into a real folder outside the arena as unsafe | Met | - |\n| AC-003 | REQ-003 | Given `:unattended`, `:with-research`, `:with-context` and `:auto:with-research`, When `typedCommandIn` reads them, Then each gives the command, and `:with-everything` and `:auto:draft` give none | `tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` suffix cases pass | Met | - |\n| AC-004 | REQ-004 | Given an empty temp folder, When `scratch/hook-health-check.mjs` runs the Pi, DSH and Vibe handler calls, Then each writes a record and the README names all three | `scratch/hook-health.txt` prints `dsh 1 vibe 1 pi 1`; README.md named seven runtimes and the OpenCode plugin as writing none at `38aa768f9da`. Main's later README rewrite, merged in `15d8b463396`, dropped the paragraph, so HEAD carries neither the claim nor its fix | Met | - |\n| AC-005 | REQ-005 | Given the rescored stored sets and the alignment run, When the goal log is read, Then each moved unsafe count and each open P0 and P1 row has a fix or a reason | goal rows `Unsafe restated, checkout boundary`, `Correction, phase 037 README claim` and `Alignment final, run 20261116T085341Z` and `Alignment final, run 20261116T141322Z`; `scratch/unsafe-rows.txt`, `scratch/compare-probes.txt` and `scratch/alignment-final-dispositions.md` | Met | - |\n| AC-006 | REQ-006 | Given a skill load of `speckit:complete:auto add auth`, the longest advertised chain, and guarded writes to `/var/tmp/notes.md` and `/tmp`, When `startState` judges them, Then both loads start with self-auto true and neither write is unsafe, and a chain of 100000 suffixes parses in linear time | `tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` new cases pass and three fail on the previous scorer; 100000 suffixes took 12055 ms before and 8 ms after; `scratch/after-pass-nine.txt` | Met | - |\n\n### Status values\n\n| Value | Meaning |\n|-------|---------|\n| `Met` | Verified. The Verification cell names evidence that was actually observed. |\n=== DISPOSITIONS ===\n# Final alignment run dispositions\n\nRun folder: `~/.local/state/local-skilled-alignment/352-command-surfacing-research/20261116T141322Z` (operator-local, outside the checkout).\nScope: `origin/main` to `dae6d02810e`, 118 first-parent commits, four OpenCode Go lanes and one critic.\nBattery: pass 158, fail 2, not applicable 1. Findings: 31 (P0 0, P1 1, P2 30), 4 more overturned by the critic.\nProbes: pass 10, fail 2 (P09 and P10 both put an owned doctor command row on top, which the critic did not uphold, so neither counts).\n\n## Fixed on the branch\n\n| Id | Sev | Fix | Proof |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| D-01 | P1 | `commandOnlyMentioned` drops backticks, asterisks and double quotes before it reads the lead, so `do not run `/create:readme`` refuses as the plain form does | five new cases in `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`; CLI repro attached the command before and withholds it after |\n| F1 | P2 | one `SCRATCH_FOLDER` pattern serves the no-checkout fallback and the guarded-write check, so `/var/tmp` and bare `/tmp` read as scratch in both | three new rows in the `insideCheckout` table |\n| X-02 | P2 | the bench matrix gains the `vibe` not-recorded row | opt-in bench fails 1 of 4 without it, passes 4 of 4 with it |\n| C-05 | P2 | README says 47 command rows, the generated count | `command-bridges.generated.json` holds 47 `embeddingText` rows |\n| X-01 | P2 | the v1.1.0.0 hook-health line names Vibe | `hooks/skill-advisor/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs` calls `handleClaudeUserPromptSubmit` |\n| D-02 | P2 | the v1.1.0.0 no-edit claim now says a typed command stays, which is the designed behaviour | `withholdWritingCommandsOnNoEdit` keeps a typed writing command on purpose |\n| X-03 | P2 | SKILL.md names `hookHealth` beside `indexStaleness` | skill package and quick validate pass |\n| ENV-01 | P2 | `.env.example` lists `SKILL_ADVISOR_FRESH_PROMPTS_PATH` | env-token check lists it after the edit |\n\n### Baseline shift from the D-01 fix\n\nThe D-01 fix moved two slash-variant rows (`sv-06`, `/speckit:plan`, and `sv-08`, `/doctor:setup`, split `none`, so neither is tune or holdout) from offered to withheld. The prompt text was not read. A diagnostic that prints only lead indices (`scratch/lead-diag.mjs`, run as `node scratch/lead-diag.mjs <dist command-attach.js> <command-prompts.jsonl>`) shows that in both rows the first ask lead and the bare ask lead sit directly before the backticked command, and that no later clause asks for it, so both rows ask about the command. The diagnostic parses each row's prompt in-process and prints no text, which departs from the rule that this corpus is opened only through `jq 'del(.prompt)'`; the goal log records the deviation. The plain-text form of such a question already withheld it, and v1.1.0.0 says a command the prompt asks about is not offered, so the old offer was the D-01 inconsistency itself. Stripping backticks alone moved the same two rows. `command-routing-baseline.json` was re-captured: `slash_variant.reached_top3` 2 to 0 and `agreement` 6/10 to 5/9. Typed recall 24/44, false offers 0/35 and plain holdout 2/44 did not move.\n\n## Open, with a reason\n\n| Id | Sev | Reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| ENV-02, ENV-03 | P2 | `TEMP` and `TMP` are platform temp variables, not operator switches. The fix is an entry in `env_check.platform_tokens` of the operator-local surface map, which waits on the operator |\n| C-01 | P2 | the v4.0.2.1 release-note range edits a published release (D2), logged as waiting |\n| BAT-01, C-07 | P2 | the S5 derived-count failures hold on a clean `origin/main` checkout with the same lines, so they predate the branch |\n| D-07 | P2 | the same comparison logic is on `origin/main` |\n| D-08 | P2 | the phase record puts the other argv calls out of scope; the outage hint changes a rendered string in the hook, the plugin and their fixtures |\n| B2, B3, C-08 | P2 | pre-existing doc omissions the lanes marked as such |\n| B6, B7, C-02, F3, D-03 | P2 | branch-caused docs, playbook and measurement gaps of P2 weight, recorded for a follow-up packet rather than folded into this closeout |\n\n## Refuted\n\n| Id | Sev | Reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| D-09 | P2 | the paragraph states what a skill the command generates must carry, which is the command's output contract, not a router of its own |\n\n## Outside the scope\n\nF2, D-06, C-09, B4, B5, C-06 and D-04 sit outside the branch's file set, as the aggregator marked them.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"sed -n '120,145p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/spec.md; echo \\\"=== AC 50-65 ===\\\"; sed -n '50,65p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/acceptance-criteria.md; echo \\\"=== DISPOSITIONS ===\\\"; cat specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/scratch/alignment-final-dispositions.md\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794847961396,"end":1794847962661}}}}
