{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794848004149,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e72ffecbrpVf6MWZonWP","part":{"partID":"prt_1e54714310014ZrBIXuA7GIjku","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e72ffecbrpVf6MWZonWP","messageID":"msg_1e546c9a9001Gy2GG05k8vvfC7","type":"tool","id":"call_a8cd869761224c398ba827e9","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n -i \"commandOnlyMentioned|mention\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/*/iterations/iteration-*.md 2>/dev/null | rg -i \"p0|p1|p2|finding\" | head -20","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-docs-8/iterations/iteration-003.md:53:- A retired name typed in a question or refusal still attaches its successor, because the typed name resolves before the mention guard reads the live name. The packet records this as an accepted limit of phase 020 (`spec.md` edge cases and decision P045), so it stays out of the active findings; iteration 3 reproduced it only to confirm no new input breaks the accepted boundary. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/020-command-offer-fit-guards/spec.md:242]\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/iterations/iteration-001.md:57:- The pass-five scope excludes `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` and the Python shim, so their command-offer and shim behavior is context, not a finding. The brief's refusal/question/history/mention check is therefore limited to the switch paths this area owns; the offer module is noted as out of scope in Ruled Out rather than silently marked covered.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/hook-close-3c/iterations/iteration-003.md:71:- **A doc that claims the contracted `make changes` form is covered.** Searched the three doc surfaces that mention the gate; none names the contracted form, so the gap is a code gap (`HC3-P1-001`), not a doc/code contradiction.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-confirm-4b/iterations/iteration-003.md:71:- The or-list constant is consumed by the same `commandOnlyMentioned` that `attachCommand` (`:491`) and the typed path call, so the P1 fix location is the shared reader, not a caller.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-close-4c/iterations/iteration-002.md:34:1. **The remediation spec still calls the question-over-an-or-list unreproduced and out of scope, and describes the carry as decline-only** -- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md:239` -- the Out of Scope line reads \"An or-list joined by `and`, `nor` or a bare comma, and a question over an or-list - no probe reproduced them (P049)\", but T029 was added after SAC4B-P2-001 reproduced that case and the shipped code now withholds the command. Assumption A3 (`:384`) repeats \"applies to the decline leads only\", the Files-to-Change row (`:248`) says \"The or-list carry for the decline leads\", and REQ-001 (`:279`) still enumerates only the three single-word refusals, so neither the requirement nor the scope text covers the article and question forms T028 and T029 added. The mechanism row (`:201`) also points at `command-attach.ts:405`, which is `:412` after T028's insertion, so the pointer no longer resolves to `commandOnlyMentioned`.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-close-4c/iterations/iteration-002.md:66:- **A hub-level regression test is missing for the article and question forms**: `attachCommand` consults only `commandOnlyMentioned` for a mention, and that predicate is pinned per form; the existing `offers no hub command for %s` row exercises the same branch, so a second row would add no distinct failure mode. Recorded as coverage commentary, not a finding.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/iterations/iteration-001.md:32:   {\"type\":\"claim\",\"claim\":\"A refusal written with the retired command name still attaches the live command because the retired-name rewrite runs before the mention guard.\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:240\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:256\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:500\"],\"counterevidenceSought\":\"Read the compiled-route path for the same prompt; it returns action defer, so the typed path is the only caller that reaches the gap, and the probe confirms that path is live.\",\"alternativeExplanation\":\"The retired name may be treated as a different command, so a refusal of the old name would not refuse the replacement. The map's own comment says the old name reads as the replacement, so the two are the same command for every other guard.\",\"finalSeverity\":\"P1\",\"confidence\":0.92,\"downgradeTrigger\":\"Downgrade to P2 if the retired name is deliberately excluded from the live command's refusal semantics.\"}\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/iterations/iteration-001.md:41:   {\"type\":\"claim\",\"claim\":\"A refusal that coordinates two command names attaches the second one because the mention reader requires a separate lead before each occurrence.\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:414\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:419\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:360\"],\"counterevidenceSought\":\"Probed the compiled route for the same prompt (defer) and the scorer rows (top skill system-deep-loop), so the typed path is the only attach. Also tested a comma variant where only one command is refused; the guard correctly leaves that one withheld.\",\"alternativeExplanation\":\"The reader may have refused only the first command and merely named the second. The prompt says 'do not run A or B', which refuses both; the same wording with 'or' is the ordinary coordinated refusal.\",\"finalSeverity\":\"P1\",\"confidence\":0.9,\"downgradeTrigger\":\"Downgrade to P2 if a coordinated refusal is judged a mention of both commands rather than a refusal of both.\"}\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/iterations/iteration-001.md:59:- `spec_code` -- partial. Phase 020's purpose says a correction inside an existing document carries no writing command; finding 3 names the generic-word path that still carries one. `REQ-004`'s two exact control prompts pass (`update the README typo in line 3` and `fix the typo in the README` return no command). Phase 024's mention reader is present and its tested cases pass; findings 1 and 2 are inputs the phase's purpose names but its tables do not cover.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/iterations/iteration-004.md:61:- **The doctor question is a `P2` from iteration 2.** Its test is the least costly of the three: one row in `QUESTION2` and one row in the `withholdMentionedCommands` table.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/iterations/iteration-002.md:34:   Finding class: mention_reader_gap\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/iterations/iteration-002.md:40:   {\"type\":\"claim\",\"claim\":\"A question or statement that puts the noun 'command' between the ask word and the command name is not recognized by the mention reader, so the command row stays passing.\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:389\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1209\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:358\"],\"counterevidenceSought\":\"Probed the direct form 'what does /doctor:update do?' and the row was withheld, so the gap is the inserted noun, not the doctor row itself. Read the ask lead list: it allows 'the command' only after 'what does/what is/...', not after the bare ask words.\",\"alternativeExplanation\":\"The question is a yes/no safety question, not a request; a command offer would still ask before writing, so the impact is an unfit offer rather than a silent write.\",\"finalSeverity\":\"P2\",\"confidence\":0.9,\"downgradeTrigger\":\"Raise to P1 if a mutating command with policy run reaches this phrasing, or if the hooks render the third row in every runtime.\"}\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-docs-8/iterations/iteration-003.md:53:- A retired name typed in a question or refusal still attaches its successor, because the typed name resolves before the mention guard reads the live name. The packet records this as an accepted limit of phase 020 (`spec.md` edge cases and decision P045), so it stays out of the active findings; iteration 3 reproduced it only to confirm no new input breaks the accepted boundary. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/020-command-offer-fit-guards/spec.md:242]\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/iterations/iteration-001.md:57:- The pass-five scope excludes `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` and the Python shim, so their command-offer and shim behavior is context, not a finding. The brief's refusal/question/history/mention check is therefore limited to the switch paths this area owns; the offer module is noted as out of scope in Ruled Out rather than silently marked covered.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/hook-close-3c/iterations/iteration-003.md:71:- **A doc that claims the contracted `make changes` form is covered.** Searched the three doc surfaces that mention the gate; none names the contracted form, so the gap is a code gap (`HC3-P1-001`), not a doc/code contradiction.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-confirm-4b/iterations/iteration-003.md:71:- The or-list constant is consumed by the same `commandOnlyMentioned` that `attachCommand` (`:491`) and the typed path call, so the P1 fix location is the shared reader, not a caller.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-close-4c/iterations/iteration-002.md:34:1. **The remediation spec still calls the question-over-an-or-list unreproduced and out of scope, and describes the carry as decline-only** -- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md:239` -- the Out of Scope line reads \"An or-list joined by `and`, `nor` or a bare comma, and a question over an or-list - no probe reproduced them (P049)\", but T029 was added after SAC4B-P2-001 reproduced that case and the shipped code now withholds the command. Assumption A3 (`:384`) repeats \"applies to the decline leads only\", the Files-to-Change row (`:248`) says \"The or-list carry for the decline leads\", and REQ-001 (`:279`) still enumerates only the three single-word refusals, so neither the requirement nor the scope text covers the article and question forms T028 and T029 added. The mechanism row (`:201`) also points at `command-attach.ts:405`, which is `:412` after T028's insertion, so the pointer no longer resolves to `commandOnlyMentioned`.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-close-4c/iterations/iteration-002.md:66:- **A hub-level regression test is missing for the article and question forms**: `attachCommand` consults only `commandOnlyMentioned` for a mention, and that predicate is pinned per form; the existing `offers no hub command for %s` row exercises the same branch, so a second row would add no distinct failure mode. Recorded as coverage commentary, not a finding.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/iterations/iteration-001.md:32:   {\"type\":\"claim\",\"claim\":\"A refusal written with the retired command name still attaches the live command because the retired-name rewrite runs before the mention guard.\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:240\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:256\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:500\"],\"counterevidenceSought\":\"Read the compiled-route path for the same prompt; it returns action defer, so the typed path is the only caller that reaches the gap, and the probe confirms that path is live.\",\"alternativeExplanation\":\"The retired name may be treated as a different command, so a refusal of the old name would not refuse the replacement. The map's own comment says the old name reads as the replacement, so the two are the same command for every other guard.\",\"finalSeverity\":\"P1\",\"confidence\":0.92,\"downgradeTrigger\":\"Downgrade to P2 if the retired name is deliberately excluded from the live command's refusal semantics.\"}\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/iterations/iteration-001.md:41:   {\"type\":\"claim\",\"claim\":\"A refusal that coordinates two command names attaches the second one because the mention reader requires a separate lead before each occurrence.\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:414\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:419\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:360\"],\"counterevidenceSought\":\"Probed the compiled route for the same prompt (defer) and the scorer rows (top skill system-deep-loop), so the typed path is the only attach. Also tested a comma variant where only one command is refused; the guard correctly leaves that one withheld.\",\"alternativeExplanation\":\"The reader may have refused only the first command and merely named the second. The prompt says 'do not run A or B', which refuses both; the same wording with 'or' is the ordinary coordinated refusal.\",\"finalSeverity\":\"P1\",\"confidence\":0.9,\"downgradeTrigger\":\"Downgrade to P2 if a coordinated refusal is judged a mention of both commands rather than a refusal of both.\"}\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/iterations/iteration-001.md:59:- `spec_code` -- partial. Phase 020's purpose says a correction inside an existing document carries no writing command; finding 3 names the generic-word path that still carries one. `REQ-004`'s two exact control prompts pass (`update the README typo in line 3` and `fix the typo in the README` return no command). Phase 024's mention reader is present and its tested cases pass; findings 1 and 2 are inputs the phase's purpose names but its tables do not cover.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/iterations/iteration-004.md:61:- **The doctor question is a `P2` from iteration 2.** Its test is the least costly of the three: one row in `QUESTION2` and one row in the `withholdMentionedCommands` table.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/iterations/iteration-002.md:34:   Finding class: mention_reader_gap\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/iterations/iteration-002.md:40:   {\"type\":\"claim\",\"claim\":\"A question or statement that puts the noun 'command' between the ask word and the command name is not recognized by the mention reader, so the command row stays passing.\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:389\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1209\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:358\"],\"counterevidenceSought\":\"Probed the direct form 'what does /doctor:update do?' and the row was withheld, so the gap is the inserted noun, not the doctor row itself. Read the ask lead list: it allows 'the command' only after 'what does/what is/...', not after the bare ask words.\",\"alternativeExplanation\":\"The question is a yes/no safety question, not a request; a command offer would still ask before writing, so the impact is an unfit offer rather than a silent write.\",\"finalSeverity\":\"P2\",\"confidence\":0.9,\"downgradeTrigger\":\"Raise to P1 if a mutating command with policy run reaches this phrasing, or if the hooks render the third row in every runtime.\"}\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"rg -n -i \\\"commandOnlyMentioned|mention\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/*/iterations/iteration-*.md 2>/dev/null | rg -i \\\"p0|p1|p2|finding\\\" | head -20\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794848003121,"end":1794848004149}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794848004162,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e72ffecbrpVf6MWZonWP","part":{"partID":"prt_1e5470ff500234YibL5dbDziSF","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e72ffecbrpVf6MWZonWP","messageID":"msg_1e546c9a9001Gy2GG05k8vvfC7","type":"tool","id":"call_d5684a3c57ff4ff7b762278f","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n -i \"single quote|single-quote|apostrophe|curly|quote mark|quoted command|backtick\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review --glob '!lineages/**' | head -30; echo \"---REPORT HEAD---\"; sed -n '1,60p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report.md","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/hook-confirm-3b/probes/command-attach-pre.ts:291:// Many keyboards type the contraction with a curly apostrophe, so the text is\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/hook-confirm-3b/iterations/iteration-002.md:109:The unchanged no-edit forms still fire: `make no changes` -> true, `make no changes, just analyze` -> true, `do not change anything` -> true, `just show me the plan` -> true, curly-apostrophe `don’t touch any files` -> true.\n---REPORT HEAD---\n# Review Report: Command Surfacing Build, Pass Nine (two lineages)\n\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder)\n- Pass: the ninth review pass. It read phase 038's net change to the scorer, the typed command matcher, the vitest config and the session tests (`85550ee946e..05f776202e0`, `review/review-scope-9.txt`, two areas).\n- Executor: `cli-opencode` with `opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash` at reasoning effort max, cap eight iterations each, threshold 0.10, stop policy convergence, through `fanout-run.cjs` (exit 0). Brief `review/review-brief-9.txt`, config `review/deep-review-fanout-config-pass-9.json`. Pass eight's report is kept as `review-report-pass-8.md`.\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\n- **Verdict: PASS.** P0 0, P1 0, P2 6, all six fixed as task T015 of phase 038.\n- **Stop: converged.** This is the first pass whose leaves ran the workflow's graph and stop steps: each iteration recorded `graphEvents`, upserted them with `upsert.cjs` and asked `convergence.cjs` for a stop decision. scorer-9 stopped at iteration 5 with `converged` (`all_dimensions_clean`), attach-config-9 at iteration 4 with `converged`. Re-running `convergence.cjs` on copies of each lineage's final state (`038 scratch/conv-scorer-9`, `conv-attach-config-9`) returns STOP `converged` `all_dimensions_clean` for both, with no failed graph signal.\n\n## 2. Findings and Dispositions\n\n| Id | Severity | Location | Finding | Disposition |\n|----|----------|----------|---------|-------------|\n| S9-P2-001 | P2 | `score-command-transcripts.mjs` `guardedWriteCounts` | `/var/tmp` and a bare scratch root counted as real folders | Fixed, two cases |\n| S9-P2-002 | P2 | `score-command-transcripts.mjs` `commandParts` | A mode typed ahead of a route stayed inside the name, so `speckit:complete:auto add auth` lost its start | Fixed: the route is split off first; the self-chosen auto check reads the name before the route too |\n| S9-P2-003 | P2 | `score-command-transcripts.mjs` `MODE_SUFFIX` | The end-anchored suffix pattern was quadratic | Fixed: known suffix words are popped one segment at a time. A chain of 100000 suffixes took 12055 ms before and 8 ms after |\n| S9-P2-004 | P2 | phase 038 | The suffix and self-auto changes had no requirement | REQ-006 and AC-006 added |\n| S9-P2-005 | P2 | `score-command-transcripts.mjs` | The modifier vocabulary was written twice, and the longest chain was untested | One `WITH_MODIFIER` source builds both patterns; the longest chain is pinned. The TypeScript matcher in `lib/command-attach.ts` keeps its own copy, since a script cannot import the runtime's source |\n| A9-P2-001 | P2 | `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | No test pinned the suffix chain's leading anchor | `/speckit:complete:draft:auto` pinned as refused |\n\n## 3. Verification\n\n`038-alignment-p1-remediation/scratch/after-pass-nine.txt`: build and typecheck exit 0, suite 2339 passed 0 failed with `AI_SESSION_CHILD` unset and set, FLOOR 24/44 0/35 2/44, EVAL [160,49,21,5], stored sets unchanged. Three new scorer cases fail on the previous scorer, and the two pins pass on both.\n\n[showing lines 29-56 of 56; full output saved to /Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/share/opencode/shell/4c10847297631c3af43d766cf1908920fe00c449/sh_1e54717f2001d7pw8i1LboDkRP.out]","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":true,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/hook-confirm-3b/probes/command-attach-pre.ts:291:// Many keyboards type the contraction with a curly apostrophe, so the text is\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/hook-confirm-3b/iterations/iteration-002.md:109:The unchanged no-edit forms still fire: `make no changes` -> true, `make no changes, just analyze` -> true, `do not change anything` -> true, `just show me the plan` -> true, curly-apostrophe `don’t touch any files` -> true.\n---REPORT HEAD---\n# Review Report: Command Surfacing Build, Pass Nine (two lineages)\n\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder)\n- Pass: the ninth review pass. It read phase 038's net change to the scorer, the typed command matcher, the vitest config and the session tests (`85550ee946e..05f776202e0`, `review/review-scope-9.txt`, two areas).\n- Executor: `cli-opencode` with `opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash` at reasoning effort max, cap eight iterations each, threshold 0.10, stop policy convergence, through `fanout-run.cjs` (exit 0). Brief `review/review-brief-9.txt`, config `review/deep-review-fanout-config-pass-9.json`. Pass eight's report is kept as `review-report-pass-8.md`.\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\n- **Verdict: PASS.** P0 0, P1 0, P2 6, all six fixed as task T015 of phase 038.\n- **Stop: converged.** This is the first pass whose leaves ran the workflow's graph and stop steps: each iteration recorded `graphEvents`, upserted them with `upsert.cjs` and asked `convergence.cjs` for a stop decision. scorer-9 stopped at iteration 5 with `converged` (`all_dimensions_clean`), attach-config-9 at iteration 4 with `converged`. Re-running `convergence.cjs` on copies of each lineage's final state (`038 scratch/conv-scorer-9`, `conv-attach-config-9`) returns STOP `converged` `all_dimensions_clean` for both, with no failed graph signal.\n\n## 2. Findings and Dispositions\n\n| Id | Severity | Location | Finding | Disposition |\n|----|----------|----------|---------|-------------|\n| S9-P2-001 | P2 | `score-command-transcripts.mjs` `guardedWriteCounts` | `/var/tmp` and a bare scratch root counted as real folders | Fixed, two cases |\n| S9-P2-002 | P2 | `score-command-transcripts.mjs` `commandParts` | A mode typed ahead of a route stayed inside the name, so `speckit:complete:auto add auth` lost its start | Fixed: the route is split off first; the self-chosen auto check reads the name before the route too |\n| S9-P2-003 | P2 | `score-command-transcripts.mjs` `MODE_SUFFIX` | The end-anchored suffix pattern was quadratic | Fixed: known suffix words are popped one segment at a time. A chain of 100000 suffixes took 12055 ms before and 8 ms after |\n| S9-P2-004 | P2 | phase 038 | The suffix and self-auto changes had no requirement | REQ-006 and AC-006 added |\n| S9-P2-005 | P2 | `score-command-transcripts.mjs` | The modifier vocabulary was written twice, and the longest chain was untested | One `WITH_MODIFIER` source builds both patterns; the longest chain is pinned. The TypeScript matcher in `lib/command-attach.ts` keeps its own copy, since a script cannot import the runtime's source |\n| A9-P2-001 | P2 | `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | No test pinned the suffix chain's leading anchor | `/speckit:complete:draft:auto` pinned as refused |\n\n## 3. Verification\n\n`038-alignment-p1-remediation/scratch/after-pass-nine.txt`: build and typecheck exit 0, suite 2339 passed 0 failed with `AI_SESSION_CHILD` unset and set, FLOOR 24/44 0/35 2/44, EVAL [160,49,21,5], stored sets unchanged. Three new scorer cases fail on the previous scorer, and the two pins pass on both.\n\n[showing lines 29-56 of 56; full output saved to /Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/share/opencode/shell/4c10847297631c3af43d766cf1908920fe00c449/sh_1e54717f2001d7pw8i1LboDkRP.out]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"rg -n -i \\\"single quote|single-quote|apostrophe|curly|quote mark|quoted command|backtick\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review --glob '!lineages/**' | head -30; echo \\\"---REPORT HEAD---\\\"; sed -n '1,60p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report.md\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794848002037,"end":1794848004162}}}}
