{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794848068972,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e72ffecbrpVf6MWZonWP","part":{"partID":"prt_1e5480c7e001s5sztNhB8sJLhP","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e72ffecbrpVf6MWZonWP","messageID":"msg_1e547e227001IiKMtbSNGAqv52","type":"tool","id":"call_d286a014b50b481f9f3accbc","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"sed -n '380,450p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs; echo \"---README MENTIONS---\"; rg -n \"capturedAtSha|captured at|clean tree|dirty\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md | head -10","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"  return colon > 1 ? command.slice(1, colon) : null;\n}\n\n// Individual rows roll up to a family only when their command names one, so a\n// command outside the `<namespace>:<name>` grammar still counts in the split\n// total without inventing a family for itself.\nfunction attachedFamilyTally(byFamily, command) {\n  const namespace = commandNamespace(command);\n  if (namespace === null) return undefined;\n  if (!byFamily.has(namespace)) {\n    byFamily.set(namespace, { tune: emptyAttachedTally(), holdout: emptyAttachedTally() });\n  }\n  return byFamily.get(namespace);\n}\n\nfunction readHeadSha(workspaceRoot) {\n  const spawned = spawnSync('git', ['rev-parse', '--short', 'HEAD'], { cwd: workspaceRoot, encoding: 'utf8' });\n  return spawned.status === 0 ? spawned.stdout.trim() : 'unknown';\n}\n\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 6. CORE LOGIC\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nexport async function scoreCommandCorpus(options = {}) {\n  const realEmbedding = options.realEmbedding === true;\n  const RealDate = Date;\n  // A harness imports this module and scores in process, so the projection must\n  // not outlive the call: every name it writes or deletes is saved here and put\n  // back in the `finally`, with an absent name deleted again.\n  const savedEnv = new Map(PROJECTED_ENV_NAMES.map((name) => [name, process.env[name]]));\n  // The projection needs an existing, empty cache directory, and that directory\n  // is scratch space this run owns. It is created before the `try` so a failure\n  // to create it has nothing left to remove, and removed in the `finally` so\n  // repeated captures do not leave one behind per run. A real capture reads the\n  // operator's own skill graph, so it owns no scratch directory and sweeps none.\n  const dbDir = realEmbedding ? null : mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'advisor-command-routing-'));\n  try {\n    // Environment projection. That empty directory makes the SQLite loader\n    // return null, so the projection is built from committed metadata alone,\n    // which is the only state a clean checkout can reproduce. A real capture reads\n    // the operator's own skill graph and embedder instead, so the three variables\n    // that select the projection are exactly the three it leaves unset.\n    if (!realEmbedding) {\n      process.env.SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR = dbDir;\n      process.env.SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLE_BUILTIN_SEMANTIC = '1';\n      // Match the test-harness regime: the semantic-shadow lane substitutes\n      // deterministic fixture vectors under the harness flag (real embeddings are\n      // not reproducible in CI), so every scorer gate runs this way. The baseline\n      // must be captured under the same regime the ratchet re-scores it in.\n      process.env.VITEST = 'true';\n    }\n    process.env.SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_FORCE_LOCAL = '1';\n    process.env.PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE = '1';\n    delete process.env.SPECKIT_ADVISOR_LANE_WEIGHTS_JSON;\n    delete process.env.SPECKIT_ADVISOR_LANE_SHADOW_WEIGHTS_JSON;\n    delete process.env.SPECKIT_ADVISOR_BM25_LEXICAL_SHADOW;\n    // Private `local-*` skills linked in through this variable live outside the\n    // checkout, so a baseline measured on a clean checkout must not see them.\n    delete process.env.SPECKIT_PRIVATE_SKILL_ROOTS;\n\n    // Pin the scoring clock to midnight UTC on the inherited scoring date.\n    const capturedAt = readPinnedScoringDate();\n    const scoringInstant = Date.parse(`${capturedAt}T00:00:00Z`);\n    globalThis.Date = class extends RealDate {\n      constructor(...args) {\n        if (args.length === 0) super(scoringInstant);\n        else super(...args);\n      }\n\n      static now() {\n---README MENTIONS---\n111:`prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs` leaves a `CLAUDE.md` holding `@AGENTS.md` in an arena that has none and appends `/CLAUDE.md` to `.git/info/exclude`, so Claude Code imports the arena's own rules while the clean-tree check and the head stay as they were. Before it copies anything it refuses the source with `source_dirty` when a tracked or untracked edit would leave the arena unlike the commit it names, with `stale_build` when a copied `dist` is older than the newest tracked file in the folder that holds it or in a folder its tsconfig `include` reaches outside that folder, and with `symlink_escape` when a link inside a copied tree resolves outside the source or names an absolute path that still resolves inside it. It writes the marker as the head, then `source clean`, then one `built <relPath> <ISO time>` line per copied build tree and one `tracked-dotenv <path>` line per tracked dotenv file.\n137:| `run-command-behaviour.mjs` | Runs one live turn per row and records the locator, exit and changed paths. `--print-argv <runtime>` prints a runtime's argv, `--list <set>` prints a set's row ids, and a run takes `--runtime` with `--set` or repeated `--row-id`, `--out <run-log>`, optional `--arm`, `--fixture` and `--dry-run`. Without `--arm`, a selection whose ids are all started-command rows runs under arm `g2`, one that holds none runs under `pre` and a mix is refused with `mixed_row_arms`. The `off` and `on` arms compare one commit with the advisor switched off and on, where a turn under either drops every inherited name that ends `_DISABLED` and holds `SKILL_ADVISOR` or `HOOKS`, and the `off` arm then sets `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED` and `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED` to `1`. `--run <n>` takes a whole number from 1 and records it on every line of that run, so two samples of one row stay apart. The `fresh` set reads `behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl` beside the script and refuses it with `fresh_missing`, `fresh_id`, `fresh_split`, `set_short`, `repeated_row`, `fresh_arm` or `fresh_run` when the file or a row breaks its rule. Each `g2` run line records the `fixture` folder its prompt named, and `--backfill` replays that folder, or `g2-fixture` beside the log for a line that holds none. `--backfill <run-log> --out <new-log> [--brief-only]` rewrites a finished log with `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offeredAs` and `briefDelivered`, or only `briefDelivered` with `--brief-only`, instead of running a turn, and prints a JSON refusal with `same_path`, `holdout_row` or `unknown_row` when it cannot. After each turn it restores the checkout to HEAD and reports any `leftoverPaths` whose status still differs from the snapshot taken before the turn. Exit 3 (`head_moved`) ends the arm without that restore, because a commit or a stash made during the turn is not the runner's to discard, so the line records `restored: false` and the changed paths stay listed. A live turn gets only the allowlisted environment, the shell basics, the locale and XDG prefixes, each runtime's own prefixes and the Skilled switch prefixes, plus the GitHub and git overrides, so no GitHub token or git credential helper from the operator's shell reaches it, and it runs with `GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL=file` so SSH and HTTPS stay out of reach. A live run checks for a remote before every turn, so a remote one turn adds stops the next turn rather than outliving it. Exit 2 refuses instead of running: bad flags, an unknown runtime or set, a holdout or unknown row, a set with fewer rows than it needs (`set_short`), a dirty worktree outside the run log's folder (`worktree_dirty`), a checkout with a git remote (`remote_present`), a checkout without the arena builder's marker (`arena_unprepared`), a selection that mixes started-command rows with others (`mixed_row_arms`), or a Codex arm whose project hook is unapproved (`codex-hooks-unapproved`). Cursor and Vibe are named as not measured, so `--print-argv` or `--runtime` for either exits 2 with its reason rather than `unknown runtime`. |\n143:| `prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs` | Builds the arena a live arm runs in: a clone of the branch tip with no remote and no outer repository, plus the ignored build trees copied in and stamped at copy time so the freshness guard reads them as fresh. It refuses a destination inside a repository or one that already exists, and skips every file whose name begins with `.env` so no secret follows the build output in. It refuses `source_dirty` when the source holds a tracked or untracked edit, `stale_build` when a copied `dist` is older than the newest tracked file in the folder that holds it or in a folder its tsconfig `include` reaches outside it, and `symlink_escape` when a link in a copied tree resolves outside the source or names an absolute path that still resolves inside it. A dotenv file the commit already tracks still arrives with the clone, so the output carries a `trackedDotenv` list naming each one and the marker writes a `tracked-dotenv <path>` line for it. The marker otherwise holds the head, `source clean` and one `built <relPath> <ISO time>` line per copied build tree. When the clone holds no `CLAUDE.md`, the builder writes one holding `@AGENTS.md` and appends `/CLAUDE.md` to `.git/info/exclude`, so Claude Code imports the arena's own rules while the clean-tree check and the head stay as they were. |\n146:| `worktree-restore.mjs` | Restores one measured turn's checkout to the snapshot taken before it, leaving a path that was already dirty alone and dropping a staged path HEAD does not know. A second snapshot after the restore reports what still differs, so the caller fails the run instead of claiming a clean worktree. |\n151:| `scorer-eval-baseline.json` | Scorer eval baseline written by `capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs`: `schemaVersion`, `capturedAt`, `capturedAtSha`, `env`, the fixture hashes and `metrics` for the full corpus, holdout, ambiguity slice, gold-none false fire, intent buckets and unknown count. The ratchet gate re-scores live under the same environment and holds every metric to it. |\n191:Exit 2 means the run was refused before or during its first prompt: bad flags, an unknown runtime or set, a holdout row, a dirty worktree outside the run log's folder, or a checkout that still has a git remote.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"  return colon > 1 ? command.slice(1, colon) : null;\n}\n\n// Individual rows roll up to a family only when their command names one, so a\n// command outside the `<namespace>:<name>` grammar still counts in the split\n// total without inventing a family for itself.\nfunction attachedFamilyTally(byFamily, command) {\n  const namespace = commandNamespace(command);\n  if (namespace === null) return undefined;\n  if (!byFamily.has(namespace)) {\n    byFamily.set(namespace, { tune: emptyAttachedTally(), holdout: emptyAttachedTally() });\n  }\n  return byFamily.get(namespace);\n}\n\nfunction readHeadSha(workspaceRoot) {\n  const spawned = spawnSync('git', ['rev-parse', '--short', 'HEAD'], { cwd: workspaceRoot, encoding: 'utf8' });\n  return spawned.status === 0 ? spawned.stdout.trim() : 'unknown';\n}\n\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 6. CORE LOGIC\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nexport async function scoreCommandCorpus(options = {}) {\n  const realEmbedding = options.realEmbedding === true;\n  const RealDate = Date;\n  // A harness imports this module and scores in process, so the projection must\n  // not outlive the call: every name it writes or deletes is saved here and put\n  // back in the `finally`, with an absent name deleted again.\n  const savedEnv = new Map(PROJECTED_ENV_NAMES.map((name) => [name, process.env[name]]));\n  // The projection needs an existing, empty cache directory, and that directory\n  // is scratch space this run owns. It is created before the `try` so a failure\n  // to create it has nothing left to remove, and removed in the `finally` so\n  // repeated captures do not leave one behind per run. A real capture reads the\n  // operator's own skill graph, so it owns no scratch directory and sweeps none.\n  const dbDir = realEmbedding ? null : mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'advisor-command-routing-'));\n  try {\n    // Environment projection. That empty directory makes the SQLite loader\n    // return null, so the projection is built from committed metadata alone,\n    // which is the only state a clean checkout can reproduce. A real capture reads\n    // the operator's own skill graph and embedder instead, so the three variables\n    // that select the projection are exactly the three it leaves unset.\n    if (!realEmbedding) {\n      process.env.SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR = dbDir;\n      process.env.SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLE_BUILTIN_SEMANTIC = '1';\n      // Match the test-harness regime: the semantic-shadow lane substitutes\n      // deterministic fixture vectors under the harness flag (real embeddings are\n      // not reproducible in CI), so every scorer gate runs this way. The baseline\n      // must be captured under the same regime the ratchet re-scores it in.\n      process.env.VITEST = 'true';\n    }\n    process.env.SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_FORCE_LOCAL = '1';\n    process.env.PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE = '1';\n    delete process.env.SPECKIT_ADVISOR_LANE_WEIGHTS_JSON;\n    delete process.env.SPECKIT_ADVISOR_LANE_SHADOW_WEIGHTS_JSON;\n    delete process.env.SPECKIT_ADVISOR_BM25_LEXICAL_SHADOW;\n    // Private `local-*` skills linked in through this variable live outside the\n    // checkout, so a baseline measured on a clean checkout must not see them.\n    delete process.env.SPECKIT_PRIVATE_SKILL_ROOTS;\n\n    // Pin the scoring clock to midnight UTC on the inherited scoring date.\n    const capturedAt = readPinnedScoringDate();\n    const scoringInstant = Date.parse(`${capturedAt}T00:00:00Z`);\n    globalThis.Date = class extends RealDate {\n      constructor(...args) {\n        if (args.length === 0) super(scoringInstant);\n        else super(...args);\n      }\n\n      static now() {\n---README MENTIONS---\n111:`prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs` leaves a `CLAUDE.md` holding `@AGENTS.md` in an arena that has none and appends `/CLAUDE.md` to `.git/info/exclude`, so Claude Code imports the arena's own rules while the clean-tree check and the head stay as they were. Before it copies anything it refuses the source with `source_dirty` when a tracked or untracked edit would leave the arena unlike the commit it names, with `stale_build` when a copied `dist` is older than the newest tracked file in the folder that holds it or in a folder its tsconfig `include` reaches outside that folder, and with `symlink_escape` when a link inside a copied tree resolves outside the source or names an absolute path that still resolves inside it. It writes the marker as the head, then `source clean`, then one `built <relPath> <ISO time>` line per copied build tree and one `tracked-dotenv <path>` line per tracked dotenv file.\n137:| `run-command-behaviour.mjs` | Runs one live turn per row and records the locator, exit and changed paths. `--print-argv <runtime>` prints a runtime's argv, `--list <set>` prints a set's row ids, and a run takes `--runtime` with `--set` or repeated `--row-id`, `--out <run-log>`, optional `--arm`, `--fixture` and `--dry-run`. Without `--arm`, a selection whose ids are all started-command rows runs under arm `g2`, one that holds none runs under `pre` and a mix is refused with `mixed_row_arms`. The `off` and `on` arms compare one commit with the advisor switched off and on, where a turn under either drops every inherited name that ends `_DISABLED` and holds `SKILL_ADVISOR` or `HOOKS`, and the `off` arm then sets `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED` and `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED` to `1`. `--run <n>` takes a whole number from 1 and records it on every line of that run, so two samples of one row stay apart. The `fresh` set reads `behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl` beside the script and refuses it with `fresh_missing`, `fresh_id`, `fresh_split`, `set_short`, `repeated_row`, `fresh_arm` or `fresh_run` when the file or a row breaks its rule. Each `g2` run line records the `fixture` folder its prompt named, and `--backfill` replays that folder, or `g2-fixture` beside the log for a line that holds none. `--backfill <run-log> --out <new-log> [--brief-only]` rewrites a finished log with `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offeredAs` and `briefDelivered`, or only `briefDelivered` with `--brief-only`, instead of running a turn, and prints a JSON refusal with `same_path`, `holdout_row` or `unknown_row` when it cannot. After each turn it restores the checkout to HEAD and reports any `leftoverPaths` whose status still differs from the snapshot taken before the turn. Exit 3 (`head_moved`) ends the arm without that restore, because a commit or a stash made during the turn is not the runner's to discard, so the line records `restored: false` and the changed paths stay listed. A live turn gets only the allowlisted environment, the shell basics, the locale and XDG prefixes, each runtime's own prefixes and the Skilled switch prefixes, plus the GitHub and git overrides, so no GitHub token or git credential helper from the operator's shell reaches it, and it runs with `GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL=file` so SSH and HTTPS stay out of reach. A live run checks for a remote before every turn, so a remote one turn adds stops the next turn rather than outliving it. Exit 2 refuses instead of running: bad flags, an unknown runtime or set, a holdout or unknown row, a set with fewer rows than it needs (`set_short`), a dirty worktree outside the run log's folder (`worktree_dirty`), a checkout with a git remote (`remote_present`), a checkout without the arena builder's marker (`arena_unprepared`), a selection that mixes started-command rows with others (`mixed_row_arms`), or a Codex arm whose project hook is unapproved (`codex-hooks-unapproved`). Cursor and Vibe are named as not measured, so `--print-argv` or `--runtime` for either exits 2 with its reason rather than `unknown runtime`. |\n143:| `prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs` | Builds the arena a live arm runs in: a clone of the branch tip with no remote and no outer repository, plus the ignored build trees copied in and stamped at copy time so the freshness guard reads them as fresh. It refuses a destination inside a repository or one that already exists, and skips every file whose name begins with `.env` so no secret follows the build output in. It refuses `source_dirty` when the source holds a tracked or untracked edit, `stale_build` when a copied `dist` is older than the newest tracked file in the folder that holds it or in a folder its tsconfig `include` reaches outside it, and `symlink_escape` when a link in a copied tree resolves outside the source or names an absolute path that still resolves inside it. A dotenv file the commit already tracks still arrives with the clone, so the output carries a `trackedDotenv` list naming each one and the marker writes a `tracked-dotenv <path>` line for it. The marker otherwise holds the head, `source clean` and one `built <relPath> <ISO time>` line per copied build tree. When the clone holds no `CLAUDE.md`, the builder writes one holding `@AGENTS.md` and appends `/CLAUDE.md` to `.git/info/exclude`, so Claude Code imports the arena's own rules while the clean-tree check and the head stay as they were. |\n146:| `worktree-restore.mjs` | Restores one measured turn's checkout to the snapshot taken before it, leaving a path that was already dirty alone and dropping a staged path HEAD does not know. A second snapshot after the restore reports what still differs, so the caller fails the run instead of claiming a clean worktree. |\n151:| `scorer-eval-baseline.json` | Scorer eval baseline written by `capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs`: `schemaVersion`, `capturedAt`, `capturedAtSha`, `env`, the fixture hashes and `metrics` for the full corpus, holdout, ambiguity slice, gold-none false fire, intent buckets and unknown count. The ratchet gate re-scores live under the same environment and holds every metric to it. |\n191:Exit 2 means the run was refused before or during its first prompt: bad flags, an unknown runtime or set, a holdout row, a dirty worktree outside the run log's folder, or a checkout that still has a git remote.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"sed -n '380,450p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs; echo \\\"---README MENTIONS---\\\"; rg -n \\\"capturedAtSha|captured at|clean tree|dirty\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md | head -10\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794848066686,"end":1794848068972}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794848069013,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e72ffecbrpVf6MWZonWP","part":{"partID":"prt_1e54810ce001teEqramoljE3Ep","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e72ffecbrpVf6MWZonWP","messageID":"msg_1e547e227001IiKMtbSNGAqv52","type":"tool","id":"call_5156387010164e68b916ecd9","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"git -c core.fsmonitor=false show 05302d03650 --stat --format='%s%n%b' | head -25; echo \"---BASELINE DIFF IN 05302---\"; git -c core.fsmonitor=false show 05302d03650 -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json | head -40","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"fix(system-skill-advisor): read a backticked command refusal as a refusal\nThe mention check now drops inline code, bold and quote marks before it reads the lead, so a refusal or a question that wraps the command in backticks withholds it as the plain wording does. Two slash-variant rows that ask about a backticked command now withhold it, and the routing baseline is re-captured for them. The scorer shares one scratch-folder pattern, the bench matrix gains its Vibe row and the advisor docs name Vibe, hookHealth, the 47 command rows and the typed-command exception to the no-edit rule.\n\nCommit-Id: 0014614\n\n\n .env.example                                       |  1 +\n .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md     |  4 +-\n .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/SKILL.md      |  2 +-\n .../system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md     |  6 +--\n .../runtime/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts |  1 +\n .../runtime/lib/command-attach.ts                  |  6 ++-\n .../runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md     |  2 +-\n .../routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json | 20 +++++-----\n .../routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs | 10 ++---\n .../runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts  | 14 +++++++\n .../tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts       |  3 ++\n .../acceptance-criteria.md                         |  2 +-\n .../graph-metadata.json                            | 19 ++++-----\n .../scratch/after-alignment-final.txt              | 20 ++++++++++\n .../scratch/alignment-final-dispositions.md        | 45 ++++++++++++++++++++++\n .../038-alignment-p1-remediation/tasks.md          |  1 +\n .../008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md            |  5 +++\n .../graph-metadata.json                            |  4 +-\n 18 files changed, 129 insertions(+), 36 deletions(-)\n---BASELINE DIFF IN 05302---\ncommit 05302d0365092f57cbe343de11f2545776251a94\nAuthor: Michel Kerkmeester <<redacted>>\nDate:   Mon Nov 16 17:05:29 2026 +0100\n\n    fix(system-skill-advisor): read a backticked command refusal as a refusal\n    \n    The mention check now drops inline code, bold and quote marks before it reads the lead, so a refusal or a question that wraps the command in backticks withholds it as the plain wording does. Two slash-variant rows that ask about a backticked command now withhold it, and the routing baseline is re-captured for them. The scorer shares one scratch-folder pattern, the bench matrix gains its Vibe row and the advisor docs name Vibe, hookHealth, the 47 command rows and the typed-command exception to the no-edit rule.\n    \n    Commit-Id: 0014614\n\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json\nindex b603c3354cf..08925294f84 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json\n@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@\n {\n   \"schemaVersion\": 1,\n   \"capturedAt\": \"2026-10-11\",\n-  \"capturedAtSha\": \"b5b8e699a97\",\n+  \"capturedAtSha\": \"dae6d02810e\",\n   \"corpusSha256\": \"sha256:e08017b5d8face375de4b51e0768fbc451e9b4d7f474e41d4ea25703ea8dcbff\",\n   \"bridgeCounts\": {\n     \"commandMetadata\": 27,\n@@ -44,14 +44,14 @@\n       \"total\": 35\n     },\n     \"slash_variant\": {\n-      \"reached_top3\": 2,\n+      \"reached_top3\": 0,\n       \"named_total\": 8,\n       \"offered_on_partial\": 0,\n       \"partial_total\": 4\n     },\n     \"agreement\": {\n-      \"correct\": 6,\n-      \"total\": 10\n+      \"correct\": 5,\n+      \"total\": 9\n     }\n   },\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"fix(system-skill-advisor): read a backticked command refusal as a refusal\nThe mention check now drops inline code, bold and quote marks before it reads the lead, so a refusal or a question that wraps the command in backticks withholds it as the plain wording does. Two slash-variant rows that ask about a backticked command now withhold it, and the routing baseline is re-captured for them. The scorer shares one scratch-folder pattern, the bench matrix gains its Vibe row and the advisor docs name Vibe, hookHealth, the 47 command rows and the typed-command exception to the no-edit rule.\n\nCommit-Id: 0014614\n\n\n .env.example                                       |  1 +\n .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md     |  4 +-\n .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/SKILL.md      |  2 +-\n .../system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md     |  6 +--\n .../runtime/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts |  1 +\n .../runtime/lib/command-attach.ts                  |  6 ++-\n .../runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md     |  2 +-\n .../routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json | 20 +++++-----\n .../routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs | 10 ++---\n .../runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts  | 14 +++++++\n .../tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts       |  3 ++\n .../acceptance-criteria.md                         |  2 +-\n .../graph-metadata.json                            | 19 ++++-----\n .../scratch/after-alignment-final.txt              | 20 ++++++++++\n .../scratch/alignment-final-dispositions.md        | 45 ++++++++++++++++++++++\n .../038-alignment-p1-remediation/tasks.md          |  1 +\n .../008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md            |  5 +++\n .../graph-metadata.json                            |  4 +-\n 18 files changed, 129 insertions(+), 36 deletions(-)\n---BASELINE DIFF IN 05302---\ncommit 05302d0365092f57cbe343de11f2545776251a94\nAuthor: Michel Kerkmeester <<redacted>>\nDate:   Mon Nov 16 17:05:29 2026 +0100\n\n    fix(system-skill-advisor): read a backticked command refusal as a refusal\n    \n    The mention check now drops inline code, bold and quote marks before it reads the lead, so a refusal or a question that wraps the command in backticks withholds it as the plain wording does. Two slash-variant rows that ask about a backticked command now withhold it, and the routing baseline is re-captured for them. The scorer shares one scratch-folder pattern, the bench matrix gains its Vibe row and the advisor docs name Vibe, hookHealth, the 47 command rows and the typed-command exception to the no-edit rule.\n    \n    Commit-Id: 0014614\n\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json\nindex b603c3354cf..08925294f84 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json\n@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@\n {\n   \"schemaVersion\": 1,\n   \"capturedAt\": \"2026-10-11\",\n-  \"capturedAtSha\": \"b5b8e699a97\",\n+  \"capturedAtSha\": \"dae6d02810e\",\n   \"corpusSha256\": \"sha256:e08017b5d8face375de4b51e0768fbc451e9b4d7f474e41d4ea25703ea8dcbff\",\n   \"bridgeCounts\": {\n     \"commandMetadata\": 27,\n@@ -44,14 +44,14 @@\n       \"total\": 35\n     },\n     \"slash_variant\": {\n-      \"reached_top3\": 2,\n+      \"reached_top3\": 0,\n       \"named_total\": 8,\n       \"offered_on_partial\": 0,\n       \"partial_total\": 4\n     },\n     \"agreement\": {\n-      \"correct\": 6,\n-      \"total\": 10\n+      \"correct\": 5,\n+      \"total\": 9\n     }\n   },\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"git -c core.fsmonitor=false show 05302d03650 --stat --format='%s%n%b' | head -25; echo \\\"---BASELINE DIFF IN 05302---\\\"; git -c core.fsmonitor=false show 05302d03650 -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json | head -40\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794848067790,"end":1794848069013}}}}
