{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794848251395,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e72ffecbrpVf6MWZonWP","part":{"partID":"prt_1e54ad22c001C6vlgKtWM93MVz","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e72ffecbrpVf6MWZonWP","messageID":"msg_1e54ac130001AcSUHPoi39P67O","type":"tool","id":"call_9067f0652ce847d7aac73f76","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- Probing the mention guard directly at HEAD with `node --import tsx` separated the quote spellings and showed the single-quote gap that the new table does not cover (iteration 1).\n- Reading `REQ-006`/`AC-006` beside the scorer diff named every changed clause and kept the scratch widening out of the findings (iteration 1).\n- Reconciling `slash_variant.reached_top3` and `agreement` against the two moved rows showed the baseline arithmetic is consistent (iteration 1).\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- Reading the first 8 `sv-*` rows only: the packet's `named_total: 8` counts eight named rows plus four partial rows, so the initial count looked short until the whole `slash_variant` set was enumerated (iteration 1).","oldString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- [First iteration -- populated as each iteration records a failed approach]","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-scorer-10/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-scorer-10/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-scorer-10/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-scorer-10/deep-revie