{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794848441095,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e72ffecbrpVf6MWZonWP","part":{"partID":"prt_1e54db8d60028EUTR2cA82Vpw0","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e72ffecbrpVf6MWZonWP","messageID":"msg_1e54d90a20016jBVzA1W4Ek4DO","type":"tool","id":"call_0614f57c42ae48a89b0b90c3","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n \"capturedAtSha|capturedAt|corpusSha256\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md | head -20; echo \"---SLICE TEST BASELINE USE---\"; sed -n '20,60p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:151:| `scorer-eval-baseline.json` | Scorer eval baseline written by `capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs`: `schemaVersion`, `capturedAt`, `capturedAtSha`, `env`, the fixture hashes and `metrics` for the full corpus, holdout, ambiguity slice, gold-none false fire, intent buckets and unknown count. The ratchet gate re-scores live under the same environment and holds every metric to it. |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:106:  readonly capturedAt: string;\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:107:  readonly capturedAtSha: string;\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:108:  readonly corpusSha256: string;\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:320:    // `capturedAtSha` is deliberately not compared: it names the commit of the\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:336:    expect(live.corpusSha256).toBe(baseline.corpusSha256);\n---SLICE TEST BASELINE USE---\n} from '../scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs';\n\nconst HERE = dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));\nconst ROUTING = resolve(HERE, '../scripts/routing-accuracy');\nconst CORPUS_PATH = join(ROUTING, 'command-prompts.jsonl');\nconst BASELINE_PATH = join(ROUTING, 'command-routing-baseline.json');\n\n// A host with its own hub vocabulary routes some rows differently from upstream.\n// It keeps its own capture in a `.host.json` file beside the upstream one, and\n// the ratchet reads that file whenever it exists. Every row stays guarded on the\n// host, including the rows its vocabulary moved.\nfunction capturePath(upstreamPath: string): string {\n  const hostPath = upstreamPath.replace(/\\.json$/, '.host.json');\n  return existsSync(hostPath) ? hostPath : upstreamPath;\n}\n\nconst BASELINE_READ_PATH = capturePath(BASELINE_PATH);\n// The capture prints its JSON to stdout, so a host writes its own file by\n// redirecting that output rather than through `--write`, which targets upstream.\nconst RECAPTURE = BASELINE_READ_PATH === BASELINE_PATH\n  ? 'node scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs --write'\n  : 'node scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs > scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.host.json';\n\n// The capture projects these nine names to score reproducibly. A harness imports\n// the module and scores in process, so the projection has to be undone before\n// the call returns or it silently changes how every later test scores.\nconst PROJECTED_ENV = [\n  'SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR',\n  'SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLE_BUILTIN_SEMANTIC',\n  'VITEST',\n  'SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_FORCE_LOCAL',\n  'PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE',\n  'SPECKIT_ADVISOR_LANE_WEIGHTS_JSON',\n  'SPECKIT_ADVISOR_LANE_SHADOW_WEIGHTS_JSON',\n  'SPECKIT_ADVISOR_BM25_LEXICAL_SHADOW',\n  'SPECKIT_PRIVATE_SKILL_ROOTS',\n] as const;\n\ntype ProjectedEnv = Readonly<Record<(typeof PROJECTED_ENV)[number], string | undefined>>;\n\nfunction readProjectedEnv(): ProjectedEnv {\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:151:| `scorer-eval-baseline.json` | Scorer eval baseline written by `capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs`: `schemaVersion`, `capturedAt`, `capturedAtSha`, `env`, the fixture hashes and `metrics` for the full corpus, holdout, ambiguity slice, gold-none false fire, intent buckets and unknown count. The ratchet gate re-scores live under the same environment and holds every metric to it. |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:106:  readonly capturedAt: string;\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:107:  readonly capturedAtSha: string;\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:108:  readonly corpusSha256: string;\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:320:    // `capturedAtSha` is deliberately not compared: it names the commit of the\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:336:    expect(live.corpusSha256).toBe(baseline.corpusSha256);\n---SLICE TEST BASELINE USE---\n} from '../scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs';\n\nconst HERE = dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));\nconst ROUTING = resolve(HERE, '../scripts/routing-accuracy');\nconst CORPUS_PATH = join(ROUTING, 'command-prompts.jsonl');\nconst BASELINE_PATH = join(ROUTING, 'command-routing-baseline.json');\n\n// A host with its own hub vocabulary routes some rows differently from upstream.\n// It keeps its own capture in a `.host.json` file beside the upstream one, and\n// the ratchet reads that file whenever it exists. Every row stays guarded on the\n// host, including the rows its vocabulary moved.\nfunction capturePath(upstreamPath: string): string {\n  const hostPath = upstreamPath.replace(/\\.json$/, '.host.json');\n  return existsSync(hostPath) ? hostPath : upstreamPath;\n}\n\nconst BASELINE_READ_PATH = capturePath(BASELINE_PATH);\n// The capture prints its JSON to stdout, so a host writes its own file by\n// redirecting that output rather than through `--write`, which targets upstream.\nconst RECAPTURE = BASELINE_READ_PATH === BASELINE_PATH\n  ? 'node scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs --write'\n  : 'node scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs > scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.host.json';\n\n// The capture projects these nine names to score reproducibly. A harness imports\n// the module and scores in process, so the projection has to be undone before\n// the call returns or it silently changes how every later test scores.\nconst PROJECTED_ENV = [\n  'SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR',\n  'SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLE_BUILTIN_SEMANTIC',\n  'VITEST',\n  'SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_FORCE_LOCAL',\n  'PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE',\n  'SPECKIT_ADVISOR_LANE_WEIGHTS_JSON',\n  'SPECKIT_ADVISOR_LANE_SHADOW_WEIGHTS_JSON',\n  'SPECKIT_ADVISOR_BM25_LEXICAL_SHADOW',\n  'SPECKIT_PRIVATE_SKILL_ROOTS',\n] as const;\n\ntype ProjectedEnv = Readonly<Record<(typeof PROJECTED_ENV)[number], string | undefined>>;\n\nfunction readProjectedEnv(): ProjectedEnv {\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"rg -n \\\"capturedAtSha|capturedAt|corpusSha256\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md | head -20; echo \\\"---SLICE TEST BASELINE USE---\\\"; sed -n '20,60p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794848438486,"end":1794848441095}}}}
