{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794848615565,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e72ffecbrpVf6MWZonWP","part":{"partID":"prt_1e55025bb001eWiu4FfduJwFxl","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e72ffecbrpVf6MWZonWP","messageID":"msg_1e54ff938001f47RKZPos3bB0v","type":"tool","id":"call_199c5cf79d814789ad533d13","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 004 - attach-scorer-10\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Mode: review, leaf iteration 4 of the `attach-scorer-10` fan-out lineage.\n- Target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder).\n- Scope: the seven `attach-scorer` rows of `review/review-scope-10.txt`.\n- Focus read first: `review/review-brief-10.txt`; this iteration answers its maintainability dimension and keeps the recorded limits (S9-P2-005 duplicate suffix vocabulary, F1 shared scratch pattern) out of the findings.\n- Prior state read: state log (three iterations), registry (AC10-P1-001 and AC10-P2-001 open), strategy (next focus: maintainability).\n- Holdout rule honoured: no prompt corpus was opened and no session text was printed.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n| File | Lines read | Dimension |\n|------|-----------|-----------|\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | 405-455 | maintainability |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | 160-195 | maintainability |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs` | 600-745, 1495-1560 | maintainability |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` | 1430-1460, 1490-1575 | maintainability |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json` | 1-60 | maintainability |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md` | 128-140 | maintainability |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts` | 20-45, 99-134 | maintainability |\n\n## Findings by Severity\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone new. AC10-P1-001 from iteration 1 stays active.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **The curly double quotes in the new strip have no test of their own** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:423` -- The strip adds `\\u201c` and `\\u201d` to the dropped set, and a typographic quote pair is a realistic paste from a word processor. The new markup table at `tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:172-184` covers backticks, asterisks and a straight double quote only, so a later simplification of the class would drop the two curly members with every test still green. The behaviour is correct today: `commandOnlyMentioned(\"what does \\u201c/create:readme\\u201d do?\", \"/create:readme\")` returns true.\n   Finding class: changed character class without a regression case.\n   Scope proof: the strip line at `:423` and the new markup table at `tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:172-184` are this area's own changed surface.\n   Affected surface hints: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:423`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:172`.\n   Case: a later edit writes the strip as `` [`*\"] `` only; every current case passes, and `what does “/create:readme” do?` starts attaching the command the reader only asked about.\n\n2. **The comment says why `_` stays but not why `'` stays, and the obvious fix for AC10-P1-001 breaks the `what's` lead** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:416` -- The new comment explains the underscore exclusion (\"a command name may hold one\") and claims \"quote marks around a name are dropped\", but the strip leaves the apostrophe in place and the fold at `:424` turns both curly single quotes into it. Nothing in the comment says why, so the natural next edit (add `'` to the strip to close the single-quote P1) silently changes `what's` to `whats`; `COMMAND_ASK_LEADS` at `:399` holds `what's` and `what is`, not `whats`, so a question written with the contraction stops being withheld.\n   Finding class: comment contract misses a load-bearing exclusion on a changed line.\n   Scope proof: the comment at `:411-418`, the strip at `:423`, the apostrophe fold at `:424` and the ask-lead list at `:399` are the same changed function and its declared vocabulary.\n   Affected surface hints: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:416`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:423`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:399`.\n   Case: a maintainer adds `'` to the strip class; the suite stays green except for whatever single-quote case they add, and `what's /speckit:plan do?` (a question with the contraction) starts attaching the command.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n- `spec_code` -- pass for this dimension. The D-01 disposition owns the mention fix, and the code implements its backtick, asterisk and double-quote clauses; the two gaps above are comment and coverage debt on that same fix, not a requirement mismatch. `REQ-006`'s scorer clauses remain matched as recorded in iteration 3.\n- `checklist_evidence` -- notApplicable; no `checklist.md` in this phase-parent packet.\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- The strip line and the comment sit at `command-attach.ts:411-424`; its two offer call sites are `:259` and `:501`, and the third consumer is `scorer/fusion.ts:1213`.\n- The markup table is `tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:172-184`; the transcript suite's new rows are `:1528-1554` and `:1438-1446`.\n- `COMMAND_ASK_LEADS` at `:399` and `COMMAND_DECLINE_LEADS` at `:379-382` are the two lists that read the folded text; the decline list already holds `dont`, which is why the apostrophe strip would break only the ask side.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- The single-quote P1 and the apostrophe comment P2 are the same character from two directions: one asks for a better fix, the other asks that the constraint behind the current omission be written down.\n- A fix for the P1 that strips only quotes adjacent to a slash command leaves `what's` and `don't` intact; a fix that strips the character everywhere does not.\n- The reversed-order suffix test gap from iteration 3 stays open as AC10-P2-001 and is not re-counted here.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- The scorer comments match the code clause by clause: the route split, the linear pop, the head-only self-auto read and the shared scratch pattern.\n- `WITH_MODIFIER` is defined once in the scorer and builds both `SUFFIX_WORD` and `SELF_AUTO`; the duplicate in `command-attach.ts` is the recorded S9-P2-005 trade-off.\n- The bench row is the exhaustive-record consequence of the runtime tuple, and the test that walks `ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES` keeps the next runtime addition honest.\n- The README cell names the two backticked rows and the 3-of-8 ceiling, consistent with the captured totals.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Re-reporting the duplicate suffix vocabulary: recorded S9-P2-005.\n- Re-reporting the shared scratch pattern: recorded F1 in the open P2 list.\n- The long README cell as a style defect: pre-existing table style, no new claim broken.\n- A stale comment on `guardedWriteCounts`: its scratch list, `..` resolution and home-path clause each match the code.\n\n## Verdict\n\nTwo new P2 findings and two active findings carried (P1 AC10-P1-001, P2 AC10-P2-001). CONDITIONAL by the active-finding mapping.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: confirmation\n- Focus area: re-read the two open P2 and the P1 against the code, then take the convergence decision\n- Reason: all four dimensions are now covered; one confirmation pass is the stabilization step before STOP\n- Rotation status: D1-D4 complete, confirmation pending\n- Required evidence: every carried finding keeps its original severity and evidence; no new direction is opened\n- Recovery note: none\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-scorer-10/iterations/iteration-004.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-scorer-10/iterations/iteration-004.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-scorer-10/iterations/iteration-004.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 004 - attach-scorer-10\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Mode: review, leaf iteration 4 of the `attach-scorer-10` fan-out lineage.\\n- Target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder).\\n- Scope: the seven `attach-scorer` rows of `review/review-scope-10.txt`.\\n- Focus read first: `review/review-brief-10.txt`; this iteration answers its maintainability dimension and keeps the recorded limits (S9-P2-005 duplicate suffix vocabulary, F1 shared scratch pattern) out of the findings.\\n- Prior state read: state log (three iterations), registry (AC10-P1-001 and AC10-P2-001 open), strategy (next focus: maintainability).\\n- Holdout rule honoured: no prompt corpus was opened and no session text was printed.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n| File | Lines read | Dimension |\\n|------|-----------|-----------|\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | 405-455 | maintainability |\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | 160-195 | maintainability |\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs` | 600-745, 1495-1560 | maintainability |\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` | 1430-1460, 1490-1575 | maintainability |\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json` | 1-60 | maintainability |\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md` | 128-140 | maintainability |\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts` | 20-45, 99-134 | maintainability |\\n\\n## Findings by Severity\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone new. AC10-P1-001 from iteration 1 stays active.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n1. **The curly double quotes in the new strip have no test of their own** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:423` -- The strip adds `\\\\u201c` and `\\\\u201d` to the dropped set, and a typographic quote pair is a realistic paste from a word processor. The new markup table at `tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:172-184` covers backticks, asterisks and a straight double quote only, so a later simplification of the class would drop the two curly members with every test still green. The behaviour is correct today: `commandOnlyMentioned(\\\"what does \\\\u201c/create:readme\\\\u201d do?\\\", \\\"/create:readme\\\")` returns true.\\n   Finding class: changed character class without a regression case.\\n   Scope proof: the strip line at `:423` and the new markup table at `tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:172-184` are this area's own changed surface.\\n   Affected surface hints: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:423`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:172`.\\n   Case: a later edit writes the strip as `` [`*\\\"] `` only; every current case passes, and `what does “/create:readme” do?` starts attaching the command the reader only asked about.\\n\\n2. **The comment says why `_` stays but not why `'` stays, and the obvious fix for AC10-P1-001 breaks the `what's` lead** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:416` -- The new comment explains the underscore exclusion (\\\"a command name may hold one\\\") and claims \\\"quote marks around a name are dropped\\\", but the strip leaves the apostrophe in place and the fold at `:424` turns both curly single quotes into it. Nothing in the comment says why, so the natural next edit (add `'` to the strip to close the single-quote P1) silently changes `what's` to `whats`; `COMMAND_ASK_LEADS` at `:399` holds `what's` and `what is`, not `whats`, so a question written with the contraction stops being withheld.\\n   Finding class: comment contract misses a load-bearing exclusion on a changed line.\\n   Scope proof: the comment at `:411-418`, the strip at `:423`, the apostrophe fold at `:424` and the ask-lead list at `:399` are the same changed function and its declared vocabulary.\\n   Affected surface hints: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:416`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:423`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:399`.\\n   Case: a maintainer adds `'` to the strip class; the suite stays green except for whatever single-quote case they add, and `what's /speckit:plan do?` (a question with the contraction) starts attaching the command.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n- `spec_code` -- pass for this dimension. The D-01 disposition owns the mention fix, and the code implements its backtick, asterisk and double-quote clauses; the two gaps above are comment and coverage debt on that same fix, not a requirement mismatch. `REQ-006`'s scorer clauses remain matched as recorded in iteration 3.\\n- `checklist_evidence` -- notApplicable; no `checklist.md` in this phase-parent packet.\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- The strip line and the comment sit at `command-attach.ts:411-424`; its two offer call sites are `:259` and `:501`, and the third consumer is `scorer/fusion.ts:1213`.\\n- The markup table is `tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:172-184`; the transcript suite's new rows are `:1528-1554` and `:1438-1446`.\\n- `COMMAND_ASK_LEADS` at `:399` and `COMMAND_DECLINE_LEADS` at `:379-382` are the two lists that read the folded text; the decline list already holds `dont`, which is why the apostrophe strip would break only the ask side.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- The single-quote P1 and the apostrophe comment P2 are the same character from two directions: one asks for a better fix, the other asks that the constraint behind the current omission be written down.\\n- A fix for the P1 that strips only quotes adjacent to a slash command leaves `what's` and `don't` intact; a fix that strips the character everywhere does not.\\n- The reversed-order suffix test gap from iteration 3 stays open as AC10-P2-001 and is not re-counted here.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- The scorer comments match the code clause by clause: the route split, the linear pop, the head-only self-auto read and the shared scratch pattern.\\n- `WITH_MODIFIER` is defined once in the scorer and builds both `SUFFIX_WORD` and `SELF_AUTO`; the duplicate in `command-attach.ts` is the recorded S9-P2-005 trade-off.\\n- The bench row is the exhaustive-record consequence of the runtime tuple, and the test that walks `ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES` keeps the next runtime addition honest.\\n- The README cell names the two backticked rows and the 3-of-8 ceiling, consistent with the captured totals.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- Re-reporting the duplicate suffix vocabulary: recorded S9-P2-005.\\n- Re-reporting the shared scratch pattern: recorded F1 in the open P2 list.\\n- The long README cell as a style defect: pre-existing table style, no new claim broken.\\n- A stale comment on `guardedWriteCounts`: its scratch list, `..` resolution and home-path clause each match the code.\\n\\n## Verdict\\n\\nTwo new P2 findings and two active findings carried (P1 AC10-P1-001, P2 AC10-P2-001). CONDITIONAL by the active-finding mapping.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: confirmation\\n- Focus area: re-read the two open P2 and the P1 against the code, then take the convergence decision\\n- Reason: all four dimensions are now covered; one confirmation pass is the stabilization step before STOP\\n- Rotation status: D1-D4 complete, confirmation pending\\n- Required evidence: every carried finding keeps its original severity and evidence; no new direction is opened\\n- Recovery note: none\\n\\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\\n\",\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-scorer-10/iterations/iteration-004.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794848597435,"end":1794848615565}}}}
