{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794848700384,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e72ffecbrpVf6MWZonWP","part":{"partID":"prt_1e5517f44001h8m99J3jDXK6ya","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e72ffecbrpVf6MWZonWP","messageID":"msg_1e5516ae1001A7VFGHraecgql5","type":"tool","id":"call_031f804eb4e243b4bf063789","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 005 - attach-scorer-10\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Mode: review, leaf iteration 5 (confirmation pass) of the `attach-scorer-10` fan-out lineage.\n- Target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder).\n- Scope: the seven `attach-scorer` rows of `review/review-scope-10.txt`.\n- Focus read first: `review/review-brief-10.txt`; this pass re-reads the four findings it produced and takes the stop decision, with no new direction opened.\n- Prior state read: state log (four iterations), registry (four open findings), strategy (all four dimensions complete).\n- Holdout rule honoured: no prompt corpus was opened and no session text was printed.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n| File | Lines read | Dimension |\n|------|-----------|-----------|\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | 395-455 | correctness, maintainability |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | 165-190 | correctness, maintainability |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs` | 609-742, 1514-1540 | correctness, traceability |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` | 1435-1450, 1520-1560 | correctness, traceability |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json` | 1-60, 1788-1812 | correctness |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md` | 134-138 | traceability |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts` | 26-36 | traceability |\n\n## Findings by Severity\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone, and no carried P0 to re-read.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone new. AC10-P1-001 is confirmed at its original severity on a re-read of the strip line, the two offer call sites and the single-quote probe.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone new. AC10-P2-001, AC10-P2-002 and AC10-P2-003 are confirmed at their original severity:\n\n- AC10-P2-001 (reversed-order suffix test): re-read `commandParts` at `:624-638` and the new cases at `:1528-1554`; the reversed chain still starts (probe unchanged) and still has no assertion.\n- AC10-P2-002 (curly double quotes untested): re-read the strip at `:423` and the markup table at `tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:172-184`; the typographic pair is stripped in code and absent from the table.\n- AC10-P2-003 (apostrophe exclusion unstated): re-probed `what's /create:readme do?` (withheld, true) and `whats /create:readme do?` (not withheld, false), which is the exact regression a blanket apostrophe strip would create.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n- `spec_code` -- pass on confirmation. `REQ-006`'s four clauses and `REQ-003`'s anchor still match the code and their cases; the D-01 disposition still matches the mention fix, with the single-quote input as its one uncovered member. No requirement row changed during the run.\n- `checklist_evidence` -- notApplicable; no `checklist.md` in this phase-parent packet.\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- Re-read the exact integration surfaces named in iterations 1-4: `attachCommand` at `command-attach.ts:501`, `typedCommandForTop` at `:259`, `fusion.ts:1213`, `insideCheckout` consumers at `score-command-transcripts.mjs:747`, `:1536`, `:1552`, the slice-test baseline pin at `command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:318-336`, and the runtime tuple at `advisor-runtime-values.ts:12-21`. No surface call path changed during the run.\n- The convergence graph now holds one dimension node per dimension, one file node per reviewed file, and one finding/evidence pair per finding, with the COVERS, IN_DIMENSION, IN_FILE and EVIDENCE_FOR edges from iterations 1-4.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- The single-quote P1 and the apostrophe comment P2 are deliberately kept as two findings: one asks for a narrower fix, the other records the constraint that makes the broad fix unsafe.\n- No new ambiguity was found; the recorded limits (suffix-before-extension, lead-diag-only baseline rows, underscore emphasis, macOS-only isolation script) still cover the adjacent cases.\n- The `capturedAtSha` question stays ruled out under the slice test's own definition at `:320`.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- Scorer: route split, linear suffix pop, head-only self-auto, shared scratch pattern, and the four `insideCheckout`/`startState` cases added for `/var/tmp` and bare `/tmp`.\n- Benchmark: the Vibe row is required by the exhaustive record and honest at `not-recorded`.\n- Baseline: the two moved rows, `reached_top3` 0, `agreement` 5/9 and `false_offer` 0/35 reconcile; the corpus hash did not move.\n- README cell: the two-backtick question claim and the 3-of-8 ceiling agree with the baseline split.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Re-opening any carried finding for a different severity: no new fact arrived in this pass.\n- A new correctness, security, traceability or maintainability direction: all four dimensions are covered and the confirmation re-read found no new input.\n- Re-reporting the recorded limits: S9-P2-005 duplicate vocabulary, F1 shared scratch pattern, and the `capturedAtSha` provenance question all stay in their recorded state.\n\n## Verdict\n\nNo new finding. Active findings: one P1 (AC10-P1-001) and three P2. The iteration final line follows the active-finding mapping and stays CONDITIONAL until the P1 is fixed.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: none remaining\n- Focus area: synthesis\n- Reason: all four dimensions are covered, both core protocols are recorded, the graph and stop steps ran on every iteration, and the only blocker to PASS is the active P1\n- Rotation status: D1-D4 complete, confirmation complete\n- Required evidence: the registry, dashboard and report must agree with this narrative\n- Recovery note: none\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-scorer-10/iterations/iteration-005.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-scorer-10/iterations/iteration-005.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-scorer-10/iterations/iteration-005.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 005 - attach-scorer-10\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Mode: review, leaf iteration 5 (confirmation pass) of the `attach-scorer-10` fan-out lineage.\\n- Target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder).\\n- Scope: the seven `attach-scorer` rows of `review/review-scope-10.txt`.\\n- Focus read first: `review/review-brief-10.txt`; this pass re-reads the four findings it produced and takes the stop decision, with no new direction opened.\\n- Prior state read: state log (four iterations), registry (four open findings), strategy (all four dimensions complete).\\n- Holdout rule honoured: no prompt corpus was opened and no session text was printed.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n| File | Lines read | Dimension |\\n|------|-----------|-----------|\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | 395-455 | correctness, maintainability |\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | 165-190 | correctness, maintainability |\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs` | 609-742, 1514-1540 | correctness, traceability |\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` | 1435-1450, 1520-1560 | correctness, traceability |\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json` | 1-60, 1788-1812 | correctness |\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md` | 134-138 | traceability |\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts` | 26-36 | traceability |\\n\\n## Findings by Severity\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone, and no carried P0 to re-read.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone new. AC10-P1-001 is confirmed at its original severity on a re-read of the strip line, the two offer call sites and the single-quote probe.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\nNone new. AC10-P2-001, AC10-P2-002 and AC10-P2-003 are confirmed at their original severity:\\n\\n- AC10-P2-001 (reversed-order suffix test): re-read `commandParts` at `:624-638` and the new cases at `:1528-1554`; the reversed chain still starts (probe unchanged) and still has no assertion.\\n- AC10-P2-002 (curly double quotes untested): re-read the strip at `:423` and the markup table at `tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:172-184`; the typographic pair is stripped in code and absent from the table.\\n- AC10-P2-003 (apostrophe exclusion unstated): re-probed `what's /create:readme do?` (withheld, true) and `whats /create:readme do?` (not withheld, false), which is the exact regression a blanket apostrophe strip would create.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n- `spec_code` -- pass on confirmation. `REQ-006`'s four clauses and `REQ-003`'s anchor still match the code and their cases; the D-01 disposition still matches the mention fix, with the single-quote input as its one uncovered member. No requirement row changed during the run.\\n- `checklist_evidence` -- notApplicable; no `checklist.md` in this phase-parent packet.\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- Re-read the exact integration surfaces named in iterations 1-4: `attachCommand` at `command-attach.ts:501`, `typedCommandForTop` at `:259`, `fusion.ts:1213`, `insideCheckout` consumers at `score-command-transcripts.mjs:747`, `:1536`, `:1552`, the slice-test baseline pin at `command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:318-336`, and the runtime tuple at `advisor-runtime-values.ts:12-21`. No surface call path changed during the run.\\n- The convergence graph now holds one dimension node per dimension, one file node per reviewed file, and one finding/evidence pair per finding, with the COVERS, IN_DIMENSION, IN_FILE and EVIDENCE_FOR edges from iterations 1-4.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- The single-quote P1 and the apostrophe comment P2 are deliberately kept as two findings: one asks for a narrower fix, the other records the constraint that makes the broad fix unsafe.\\n- No new ambiguity was found; the recorded limits (suffix-before-extension, lead-diag-only baseline rows, underscore emphasis, macOS-only isolation script) still cover the adjacent cases.\\n- The `capturedAtSha` question stays ruled out under the slice test's own definition at `:320`.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- Scorer: route split, linear suffix pop, head-only self-auto, shared scratch pattern, and the four `insideCheckout`/`startState` cases added for `/var/tmp` and bare `/tmp`.\\n- Benchmark: the Vibe row is required by the exhaustive record and honest at `not-recorded`.\\n- Baseline: the two moved rows, `reached_top3` 0, `agreement` 5/9 and `false_offer` 0/35 reconcile; the corpus hash did not move.\\n- README cell: the two-backtick question claim and the 3-of-8 ceiling agree with the baseline split.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- Re-opening any carried finding for a different severity: no new fact arrived in this pass.\\n- A new correctness, security, traceability or maintainability direction: all four dimensions are covered and the confirmation re-read found no new input.\\n- Re-reporting the recorded limits: S9-P2-005 duplicate vocabulary, F1 shared scratch pattern, and the `capturedAtSha` provenance question all stay in their recorded state.\\n\\n## Verdict\\n\\nNo new finding. Active findings: one P1 (AC10-P1-001) and three P2. The iteration final line follows the active-finding mapping and stays CONDITIONAL until the P1 is fixed.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: none remaining\\n- Focus area: synthesis\\n- Reason: all four dimensions are covered, both core protocols are recorded, the graph and stop steps ran on every iteration, and the only blocker to PASS is the active P1\\n- Rotation status: D1-D4 complete, confirmation complete\\n- Required evidence: the registry, dashboard and report must agree with this narrative\\n- Recovery note: none\\n\\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\\n\",\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-scorer-10/iterations/iteration-005.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794848685892,"end":1794848700384}}}}
