{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794848892267,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e72ffecbrpVf6MWZonWP","part":{"partID":"prt_1e5547134001lgDmhUbGRthfBR","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e72ffecbrpVf6MWZonWP","messageID":"msg_1e5543d9f001zMTISw0tS6We13","type":"tool","id":"call_44f86fe958a74dbca5f9fd83","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 007 - attach-scorer-10\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Mode: review, leaf iteration 7 (stuck recovery: escalate-severity review) of the `attach-scorer-10` fan-out lineage.\n- Recovery entry: `stuckRecovery` from iteration 6 (`stuckThresholdReached`), recorded through the append gateway as `deep_review.recovery_started` with strategy `escalate-severity-review`, target dimension correctness.\n- Target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder).\n- Scope: the seven `attach-scorer` rows of `review/review-scope-10.txt`.\n- Focus read first: `review/review-brief-10.txt`; this pass changes granularity from cross-reference to an explicit P0/P1 hunt over the carried findings and their call paths.\n- Holdout rule honoured: no prompt corpus was opened and no session text was printed.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n| File | Lines read | Dimension |\n|------|-----------|-----------|\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | 240-270, 330-455, 480-520 | correctness |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | 160-240, 455-485 | correctness |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs` | 700-760, 1355-1375, 1495-1545 | correctness |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` | 1430-1575 | correctness |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json` | 44-56, 1788-1812 | correctness |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md` | 134 | correctness |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts` | 26-36 | correctness |\n\n## Findings by Severity\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone. The escalation hunt asked whether an offer on a refused prompt can execute anything by itself, and it cannot: `attachCommand` returns a command string on a recommendation, `typedCommandForTop` returns a typed command record, and no path in the area executes, writes, or bypasses a policy. There is no data-loss, auth-bypass or destructive-action path in the seven files.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone new. AC10-P1-001 remains P1 and is not P0: the worst outcome is an unwanted offer of a command the reader refused, and the command's own policy still governs whether it starts; the defect does not auto-run or auto-write.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone new. The three open P2 keep their severity: each is a coverage or comment gap on code whose current behaviour is correct, so none reaches the P1 bar.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n- `spec_code` -- pass on the escalation read: `REQ-006` and `REQ-003` still match their code and cases, and the D-01 disposition still owns the mention fix with the single-quote input uncovered.\n- `checklist_evidence` -- notApplicable; no `checklist.md` in this phase-parent packet.\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- Escalation call-path check: `commandOnlyMentioned` is consulted at `command-attach.ts:259` and `:501` and at `scorer/fusion.ts:1213`, `:1232`, `:1248`; every one returns a recommendation or a command record. No caller writes, starts, or executes from the predicate.\n- Guarded-write call path: `startState` at `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1500` computes `unsafe` from `selfAuto || (guarded && wrote)`, and `started` from `touched && shape !== 'readOnly'`; no write is performed by the reader.\n- The two severity questions (P1 not P0, P2 not P1) were each answered from these call paths, not from the finding text.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Recovery pass: the last two iterations were zero-finding and the stuck threshold fired, so this pass deliberately searched for a missed P0/P1 and for an over-rated P2 rather than repeating the cross-reference read. No change to the finding set followed.\n- A refused command that carries a `run` policy is still only offered; the host decides to start it, so the P1 impact stays an unfit offer.\n- The single-quote gap and the apostrophe comment remain linked but separately rated, as recorded in iteration 4.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- No P0 class exists in the changed surfaces: no destructive write, no auth or policy bypass, no secret handling, no filesystem execution.\n- The scorer's `unsafe` flag is a measurement and cannot itself start or stop a run.\n- The bench and README changes carry no behavioural path.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Escalating AC10-P1-001 to P0: no automatic execution follows the offer.\n- Escalating any P2 to P1: each gap leaves today's behaviour correct.\n- Re-opening the recorded limits or the `capturedAtSha` question.\n\n## Verdict\n\nNo new finding. Active findings remain one P1 and three P2; CONDITIONAL by the active-finding mapping.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: none remaining\n- Focus area: stop decision, then synthesis\n- Reason: the recovery pass confirmed the finding set and all four dimensions are covered\n- Rotation status: D1-D4 complete; recovery complete\n- Required evidence: the next convergence decision is a STOP before synthesis\n- Recovery note: the escalation strategy was applied and produced no severity change\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-scorer-10/iterations/iteration-007.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-scorer-10/iterations/iteration-007.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-scorer-10/iterations/iteration-007.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 007 - attach-scorer-10\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Mode: review, leaf iteration 7 (stuck recovery: escalate-severity review) of the `attach-scorer-10` fan-out lineage.\\n- Recovery entry: `stuckRecovery` from iteration 6 (`stuckThresholdReached`), recorded through the append gateway as `deep_review.recovery_started` with strategy `escalate-severity-review`, target dimension correctness.\\n- Target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder).\\n- Scope: the seven `attach-scorer` rows of `review/review-scope-10.txt`.\\n- Focus read first: `review/review-brief-10.txt`; this pass changes granularity from cross-reference to an explicit P0/P1 hunt over the carried findings and their call paths.\\n- Holdout rule honoured: no prompt corpus was opened and no session text was printed.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n| File | Lines read | Dimension |\\n|------|-----------|-----------|\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | 240-270, 330-455, 480-520 | correctness |\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | 160-240, 455-485 | correctness |\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs` | 700-760, 1355-1375, 1495-1545 | correctness |\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` | 1430-1575 | correctness |\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json` | 44-56, 1788-1812 | correctness |\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md` | 134 | correctness |\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts` | 26-36 | correctness |\\n\\n## Findings by Severity\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone. The escalation hunt asked whether an offer on a refused prompt can execute anything by itself, and it cannot: `attachCommand` returns a command string on a recommendation, `typedCommandForTop` returns a typed command record, and no path in the area executes, writes, or bypasses a policy. There is no data-loss, auth-bypass or destructive-action path in the seven files.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone new. AC10-P1-001 remains P1 and is not P0: the worst outcome is an unwanted offer of a command the reader refused, and the command's own policy still governs whether it starts; the defect does not auto-run or auto-write.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\nNone new. The three open P2 keep their severity: each is a coverage or comment gap on code whose current behaviour is correct, so none reaches the P1 bar.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n- `spec_code` -- pass on the escalation read: `REQ-006` and `REQ-003` still match their code and cases, and the D-01 disposition still owns the mention fix with the single-quote input uncovered.\\n- `checklist_evidence` -- notApplicable; no `checklist.md` in this phase-parent packet.\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- Escalation call-path check: `commandOnlyMentioned` is consulted at `command-attach.ts:259` and `:501` and at `scorer/fusion.ts:1213`, `:1232`, `:1248`; every one returns a recommendation or a command record. No caller writes, starts, or executes from the predicate.\\n- Guarded-write call path: `startState` at `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1500` computes `unsafe` from `selfAuto || (guarded && wrote)`, and `started` from `touched && shape !== 'readOnly'`; no write is performed by the reader.\\n- The two severity questions (P1 not P0, P2 not P1) were each answered from these call paths, not from the finding text.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Recovery pass: the last two iterations were zero-finding and the stuck threshold fired, so this pass deliberately searched for a missed P0/P1 and for an over-rated P2 rather than repeating the cross-reference read. No change to the finding set followed.\\n- A refused command that carries a `run` policy is still only offered; the host decides to start it, so the P1 impact stays an unfit offer.\\n- The single-quote gap and the apostrophe comment remain linked but separately rated, as recorded in iteration 4.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- No P0 class exists in the changed surfaces: no destructive write, no auth or policy bypass, no secret handling, no filesystem execution.\\n- The scorer's `unsafe` flag is a measurement and cannot itself start or stop a run.\\n- The bench and README changes carry no behavioural path.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- Escalating AC10-P1-001 to P0: no automatic execution follows the offer.\\n- Escalating any P2 to P1: each gap leaves today's behaviour correct.\\n- Re-opening the recorded limits or the `capturedAtSha` question.\\n\\n## Verdict\\n\\nNo new finding. Active findings remain one P1 and three P2; CONDITIONAL by the active-finding mapping.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: none remaining\\n- Focus area: stop decision, then synthesis\\n- Reason: the recovery pass confirmed the finding set and all four dimensions are covered\\n- Rotation status: D1-D4 complete; recovery complete\\n- Required evidence: the next convergence decision is a STOP before synthesis\\n- Recovery note: the escalation strategy was applied and produced no severity change\\n\\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\\n\",\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-scorer-10/iterations/iteration-007.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794848878900,"end":1794848892267}}}}
